// python/points-to: Python's call targets and value types, in the analysis phase (P3 of decision 0083 §1, note t28).
//
// Interface: call_target, call_open (python/calls), type_of, type_open, proven_type, possible_type, possible_open
// (python/types). Every other relation here is this module's own, named `pt_…`.
//
// It reads the earlier phases' exports (`struct__…`, P1's structure; `types__…`, P2's declared types), which the
// engine runs before the program that reads them, so a rule that includes this reads libraries only through them,
// by symbol. It is the analysis program's own fixpoint, beside the rules that read it: no program of its own, and
// no answers carried in as facts (the `typing_calls__` bridge it replaces).
//
// What follows was calls_p3.rerail's header (that program now includes this module).
// calls_p3.rerail: the analysis phase. calls_cx.rerail's call targets and types over the
// workspace's documents alone: no library document is loaded, and no rule here loads one. A library is read only
// through what the typing phase (types.rerail, P2, over struct.rerail's P1) hands on, keyed by symbol.
//
// So values are of two sorts. A workspace value is a node, as in calls_cx (`pt_pv(n, k, v)`): this phase parses the
// workspace, and reads another document's values by symbol (`pt_wres`). A library value is a symbol (`pt_lv(n, k, s)`: n may be the library's s, of kind k):
//   - a name an import binds, resolved through `types__binds` (`lres`), whose module is not the workspace's;
//   - a builtin name, a literal (`builtins.int`), an attribute of a library module, class or instance
//     (`types__attr`, through the class's bases), a library class's call (its instance), a library function's call
//     (its declared return's head, `types__rtype`), an implicit call (`__iter__`, `__getitem__`) on a library
//     instance;
//   - a workspace class's library base (`lbase`): what the workspace class does not bind, the base answers.
// Library values flow back into workspace values where a library declares it: a decorator declared `(f: F) -> F`
// keeps the definition, one declared `(f: Callable[P, A]) -> Callable[P, B]` wraps it (`contextmanager`), a method
// declared `-> Self` returns its receiver.
//
// What calls_cx reads from a library's nodes and this does not yet: generic instantiation through a library's
// classes (`list[C]`'s `__iter__`, `dict[str, C].get`), overloads fitted by arity (every overload's return is
// taken), and `async def` in stubs. Those values are unknown here (`vopen`), never wrong.
//
// What follows is calls_cx.rerail's header.
// calls_cx.rerail (P3's source): calls.rerail with every cross-file lookup a function of the reader's import closure (decision 0076, O114),
// so its fixpoint can be memoised per import component. Generated from calls.rerail by
// fixtures/python/calls/make_cx.py; edit calls.rerail and regenerate. What differs:
// - a module's bindings (`qv`, `tqv`, `qopen`) are keyed by the module's symbols. Here (t32 stage 8) a reader finds
//   them by the symbol P2 resolves its name to (`pt_wres`), with no import closure of P3's own;
// - attribute lookups are keyed by the node that asks (`asks`, `fv`, `attr_open`), not by the class asked, and
//   `found` is not cut to the names some reader asks for;
// - closed-world `self` and annotations reach the subclasses in the reader's closure (here: every workspace
//   subclass);
// - subtyping (`tsub`, `tsup_open`) is per node;
// - generics' heads (`ghead`, `ghcls`) are made for every subscript argument, an instance attribute's assignment
//   (`iattr`) is keyed by the assignment, and a star import binds every public name, not what importers want.
// Call-target resolution and call chains for Python, in Rerail's Datalog dialect.
//
// One points-to relation, `pt_pv(n, kind, v)`: expression n may evaluate to v, a function (`fn`, a function_definition),
// a class object (`cls`), an instance of a class (`inst`), a module (`mod`), or `super()` in a class (`super`).
// `pt_vopen(n)`: n may also evaluate to something no static name denotes. A call's answer is three-valued, as the
// native `calls` relation's is: `call_open` (unknown), else the definitions `call_target` names (none: no edge).
//
// Python semantics covered: LEGB scope lookup (class scopes are invisible to nested functions), imports (absolute,
// relative (any number of dots), aliased, star, function-local), re-exports through module bindings, later unconditional bindings
// shadowing earlier ones, decorators (transparent ones, workspace decorators through their returns, others unknown),
// classes and inheritance (method lookup through bases, constructors to `__init__`, instances to `__call__`),
// late-bound `self`/`cls` (the class and every workspace subclass), `super()`, and function values flowing through
// assignments, returns and a function's returned parameter.
// Its cross-file part is one fixpoint over every loaded document, as any program's is (decision 0065).

// Guests (decision 0055): parsed(s, "annotation", r) asks for string s's code, rooted at r; host_node(n, h): h is
// the innermost host node over guest node n. A quoted annotation's code is the annotation context's (decision 0597,
// python/annotation): its instance of these rules reads its trees, and the host reads what it exports (below
// pt_aopen).
// The run's settings (the Python version and platform a branch is decided by, python/conditions.rerail). No library
// is loaded: the imports are resolved, and the libraries loaded, by phase 1 (sources.rerail).
#include "core.rerail"
#include "python/conditions.rerail"
#include "python/annotation.rerail"
// What the earlier phases hand on (struct.rerail, types.rerail): every document's structure, the workspace's and the
// libraries' its imports reach, by symbol.
.decl struct__def(s: symbol, k: symbol)
.decl struct__base(c: symbol, i: number, b: symbol)
.decl struct__flag(f: symbol, k: symbol)
.decl struct__shape(f: symbol, need: number, cap: number, kw: number)
.decl types__binds(m: symbol, x: symbol, d: symbol)
.decl types__attr(c: symbol, x: symbol, d: symbol, k: symbol)
.decl types__owner(s: symbol, m: symbol)
.decl types__sig(f: symbol, i: number, x: symbol, a: symbol, d: symbol)
.decl types__rtype(f: symbol, a: symbol, d: symbol)
.decl types__vtype(s: symbol, a: symbol, d: symbol)
.decl types__callret(f: symbol, b: symbol, d: symbol)
.decl types__tparam(c: symbol, i: number, y: symbol)
.decl types__tmap(k: symbol, i: number, a: symbol, y: symbol)
.decl types__rvar(f: symbol, y: symbol)
.decl types__rgen(f: symbol, k: symbol, j: number, y: symbol)
.decl types__ropen(f: symbol)
.decl types__wgen(f: symbol, ka: symbol, i: number, kb: symbol, j: number)
.decl types__pgen(f: symbol, i: number, k: symbol, j: number, y: symbol)
.decl types__rcarg(f: symbol, k: symbol, j: number, d: symbol)
.decl types__anc(c: symbol, a: symbol)
.decl types__proto(c: symbol)
.decl struct__param(f: symbol, i: number, x: symbol, a: symbol)
// No import closure (t32 stage 8): a name another document binds is resolved by P2 (`types__binds`, `types__attr`) to
// a symbol, and read by that symbol (`pt_wres`). A class's late-bound `self`, and a declared class's values, are the
// class and each workspace subclass.

.decl pt_scope(kind: symbol)
pt_scope("module"). pt_scope("function_definition"). pt_scope("class_definition"). pt_scope("lambda").
// What a name in a scope sees when its own scope does not bind it: class scopes are skipped.
.decl pt_fscope(kind: symbol)
pt_fscope("module"). pt_fscope("function_definition"). pt_fscope("lambda").
.decl pt_fdef(kind: symbol)
pt_fdef("function_definition").

.decl pt_modnode(d: number, m: node)
pt_modnode(d, m) :- node(d, m, "module", _, _).
.decl pt_modname(m: node, q: symbol)
pt_modname(m, q) :- pt_modnode(d, m), doc(d, _, q).

// ---- names read, and the scope that binds them ----------------------------------------------------------------
.decl pt_nameref(n: node, x: symbol)
pt_nameref(n, x) :- kind(n, "identifier"), text(n, x), !field(_, "attribute", n), !field(_, "name", n).
.decl pt_rdefn(s: node, x: symbol, f: node)
pt_rdefn(s, x, f) :- kind(f, "function_definition"), field(f, "name", nm), text(nm, x), nearest(f, s, pt_scope), !py_dead_at(f).
pt_rdefn(s, x, f) :- kind(f, "class_definition"), field(f, "name", nm), text(nm, x), nearest(f, s, pt_scope), !py_dead_at(f).
.decl pt_rasg(s: node, x: symbol, r: node, a: node)
pt_rasg(s, x, r, a) :- kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", l), kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, x), field(a, "right", r), nearest(a, s, pt_scope), !py_dead_at(a).
// `for x in it`: x is bound to the loop target's value, `it.__iter__().__next__()` (implicit calls, `icall`); `with e
// as x`: to the alias's, `e.__enter__()`. Their `async` forms await `it.__aiter__().__anext__()` and `e.__aenter__()`
// (`iawait`).
pt_rasg(s, x, l, a) :- kind(a, "for_statement"), field(a, "left", l), kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, x), nearest(a, s, pt_scope),
    !py_dead_at(a).
pt_rasg(s, x, t, a) :- kind(a, "with_statement"), child(a, wc, _), child(wc, w, _), kind(w, "with_item"), field(w, "value", p),
    kind(p, "as_pattern"), field(p, "alias", t), child(t, i, 0), kind(i, "identifier"), text(i, x), nearest(a, s, pt_scope), !py_dead_at(a).
.decl pt_param(f: node, x: symbol, i: number)
pt_param(f, x, i) :- field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, i), kind(p, "identifier"), text(p, x).
pt_param(f, x, i) :- field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, i), child(p, id, 0), kind(id, "identifier"), text(id, x).
// Targets whose value is not tracked: patterns, loop and comprehension variables, `with`/`except` names, walrus,
// augmented assignment, and names a `global`/`nonlocal` declaration hands to another scope.
.decl pt_patkind(k: symbol)
pt_patkind("pattern_list"). pt_patkind("tuple_pattern"). pt_patkind("list_pattern"). pt_patkind("list_splat_pattern").
pt_patkind("parenthesized_expression"). pt_patkind("tuple"). pt_patkind("list"). pt_patkind("expression_list").
.decl pt_tgt(t: node)
pt_tgt(l) :- kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", l), !kind(l, "identifier").
pt_tgt(l) :- kind(a, "augmented_assignment"), field(a, "left", l).
pt_tgt(l) :- kind(a, "for_statement"), field(a, "left", l), !kind(l, "identifier").
pt_tgt(l) :- kind(a, "for_in_clause"), field(a, "left", l).
pt_tgt(l) :- kind(a, "named_expression"), field(a, "name", l).
pt_tgt(l) :- kind(l, "as_pattern_target").
pt_tgt(c) :- pt_tgt(t), kind(t, k), pt_patkind(k), child(t, c, _).
pt_tgt(c) :- pt_tgt(t), kind(t, "as_pattern_target"), child(t, c, _), !pt_wtgt(t).
// A `with` alias bound by `rasg`.
.decl pt_wtgt(t: node)
pt_wtgt(t) :- pt_rasg(_, _, t, a), kind(a, "with_statement").
.decl pt_rotgt(s: node, x: symbol)
pt_rotgt(s, x) :- pt_tgt(t), kind(t, "identifier"), text(t, x), nearest(t, s, pt_scope).

// Imports, per scope: `pt_ibind(s, x, q)` binds x to the qualified name q; `ifrom` also keeps the module and name.
.decl pt_impmod(i: node, m: symbol)
pt_impmod(i, m) :- kind(i, "import_from_statement"), field(i, "module_name", mn), kind(mn, "dotted_name"), text(mn, m), !py_dead_at(i).
pt_impmod(i, p) :- kind(i, "import_from_statement"), field(i, "module_name", mn), kind(mn, "relative_import"),
    child(mn, pre, 0), text(pre, "."), !child(mn, _, 1), docof(i, d), pkg(d, p), p != "", !py_dead_at(i).
pt_impmod(i, @dot(p, m)) :- kind(i, "import_from_statement"), field(i, "module_name", mn), kind(mn, "relative_import"),
    child(mn, pre, 0), text(pre, "."), child(mn, dn, 1), text(dn, m), docof(i, d), pkg(d, p), p != "", !py_dead_at(i).
.decl pt_rifrom(s: node, x: symbol, m: symbol, y: symbol)
pt_rifrom(s, y, m, y) :- pt_impmod(i, m), field(i, "name", n), kind(n, "dotted_name"), text(n, y), nearest(i, s, pt_scope).
pt_rifrom(s, a, m, y) :- pt_impmod(i, m), field(i, "name", x), kind(x, "aliased_import"), field(x, "name", n), text(n, y),
    field(x, "alias", al), text(al, a), nearest(i, s, pt_scope).
.decl pt_ribind(s: node, x: symbol, q: symbol)
pt_ribind(s, x, @dot(m, y)) :- pt_rifrom(s, x, m, y).
pt_ribind(s, t, t) :- kind(i, "import_statement"), field(i, "name", n), kind(n, "dotted_name"), child(n, c, 0), text(c, t), nearest(i, s, pt_scope), !py_dead_at(i).
pt_ribind(s, a, m) :- kind(i, "import_statement"), field(i, "name", x), kind(x, "aliased_import"), field(x, "name", n), text(n, m),
    field(x, "alias", al), text(al, a), nearest(i, s, pt_scope), !py_dead_at(i).
// Two dots or more: `..` is the package's parent (`from .. import x` in `pkg.sub.deep` is `pkg`), one level up per dot.
.decl pt_updots(t: symbol, k: number)
pt_updots("..", 1). pt_updots("...", 2). pt_updots("....", 3).
pt_impmod(i, q) :- kind(i, "import_from_statement"), field(i, "module_name", mn), kind(mn, "relative_import"),
    child(mn, pre, 0), text(pre, t), pt_updots(t, k), !child(mn, _, 1), docof(i, d), pkg(d, p), q = @pkg_up(p, k), q != "", !py_dead_at(i).
pt_impmod(i, @dot(q, m)) :- kind(i, "import_from_statement"), field(i, "module_name", mn), kind(mn, "relative_import"),
    child(mn, pre, 0), text(pre, t), pt_updots(t, k), child(mn, dn, 1), text(dn, m), docof(i, d), pkg(d, p),
    q = @pkg_up(p, k), q != "", !py_dead_at(i).
// A relative import the facts cannot place (more dots than packages, or outside a package): what it binds is unknown.
.decl pt_irel_open(i: node)
pt_irel_open(i) :- kind(i, "import_from_statement"), field(i, "module_name", mn), kind(mn, "relative_import"), !pt_impmod(i, _).
pt_rotgt(s, y) :- pt_irel_open(i), field(i, "name", n), kind(n, "dotted_name"), text(n, y), nearest(i, s, pt_scope).
pt_rotgt(s, a) :- pt_irel_open(i), field(i, "name", x), kind(x, "aliased_import"), field(x, "alias", al), text(al, a), nearest(i, s, pt_scope).
.decl pt_star(s: node)
pt_star(s) :- kind(i, "import_from_statement"), child(i, w, _), kind(w, "wildcard_import"), nearest(i, s, pt_scope).

// `global x` / `nonlocal x`: the scope's bindings of x are the module's / the enclosing function's.
.decl pt_decl(s: node, x: symbol, t: node)
pt_decl(s, x, m) :- kind(g, "global_statement"), child(g, i, _), text(i, x), nearest(g, s, pt_scope), docof(g, d), pt_modnode(d, m).
pt_decl(s, x, p) :- kind(g, "nonlocal_statement"), child(g, i, _), text(i, x), nearest(g, s, pt_scope), nearest(s, p, pt_fscope).
.decl pt_rbound(s: node, x: symbol)
pt_rbound(s, x) :- pt_rdefn(s, x, _).
pt_rbound(s, x) :- pt_rasg(s, x, _, _).
pt_rbound(s, x) :- pt_rotgt(s, x).
pt_rbound(s, x) :- pt_ribind(s, x, _).
.decl pt_home(s: node, x: symbol, t: node)
pt_home(s, x, s) :- pt_rbound(s, x), !pt_decl(s, x, _).
pt_home(s, x, t) :- pt_rbound(s, x), pt_decl(s, x, t).
.decl pt_defn(s: node, x: symbol, f: node)
pt_defn(t, x, f) :- pt_rdefn(s, x, f), pt_home(s, x, t).
.decl pt_asg(s: node, x: symbol, r: node, a: node)
pt_asg(t, x, r, a) :- pt_rasg(s, x, r, a), pt_home(s, x, t).
.decl pt_otgt(s: node, x: symbol)
pt_otgt(t, x) :- pt_rotgt(s, x), pt_home(s, x, t).
.decl pt_ifrom(s: node, x: symbol, m: symbol, y: symbol)
pt_ifrom(t, x, m, y) :- pt_rifrom(s, x, m, y), pt_home(s, x, t).
.decl pt_ibind(s: node, x: symbol, q: symbol)
pt_ibind(t, x, q) :- pt_ribind(s, x, q), pt_home(s, x, t).

.decl pt_bound_in(s: node, x: symbol)
pt_bound_in(s, x) :- pt_defn(s, x, _).
pt_bound_in(s, x) :- pt_asg(s, x, _, _).
pt_bound_in(f, x) :- pt_param(f, x, _).
pt_bound_in(s, x) :- pt_otgt(s, x).
pt_bound_in(s, x) :- pt_ibind(s, x, _).

// LEGB: from the nearest scope outwards, skipping class scopes, to the first that binds the name.
.decl pt_walk(n: node, x: symbol, s: node)
pt_walk(n, x, s) :- pt_nameref(n, x), nearest(n, s, pt_scope), !host_node(n, _).
// A name in a guest (a quoted annotation's code) is looked up from the string that holds it (pt_hstart), and steps
// through the host's scopes (pt_up: a module has no step), which the annotation context reads finished.
pt_walk(n, x, s) :- pt_nameref(n, x), host_node(n, h), pt_hstart(h, s).
pt_walk(n, x, p) :- pt_walk(n, x, s), !pt_bound_in(s, x), pt_up(s, p).
.decl pt_hstart(h: node, s: node)
pt_hstart(h, s) :- ann_host(h, t), nearest(t, s, pt_scope).   // h: a tree's host node (python/annotation)
.decl pt_up(s: node, p: node)
pt_up(s, p) :- kind(s, k), pt_scope(k), nearest(s, p, pt_fscope).
.decl pt_look(n: node, x: symbol, s: node)
pt_look(n, x, s) :- pt_walk(n, x, s), pt_bound_in(s, x).
// Bound nowhere: a builtin, or (a star import, `globals()`) unknown.
.decl pt_miss(n: node, x: symbol)
pt_miss(n, x) :- pt_walk(n, x, m), !pt_up(m, _), !pt_bound_in(m, x).
.decl pt_builtin_ref(n: node, x: symbol)
pt_builtin_ref(n, x) :- pt_miss(n, x), pt_builtin(x), docof(n, d), pt_modnode(d, m), !pt_star(m).

// ---- unconditional rebinding --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// A statement of a scope's own body (not inside an `if`, loop or `try`) binding x; a later one replaces an earlier one.
.decl pt_stmt(st: node, s: node)
pt_stmt(st, s) :- kind(s, "module"), child(s, st, _).
pt_stmt(st, s) :- kind(s, "function_definition"), field(s, "body", b), child(b, st, _).
pt_stmt(st, s) :- kind(s, "class_definition"), field(s, "body", b), child(b, st, _).
.decl pt_defstmt(f: node, st: node)
pt_defstmt(f, f) :- kind(f, "function_definition").
pt_defstmt(f, f) :- kind(f, "class_definition").
pt_defstmt(f, st) :- kind(st, "decorated_definition"), field(st, "definition", f).
.decl pt_asgstmt(a: node, st: node)
pt_asgstmt(a, st) :- kind(st, "expression_statement"), child(st, a, 0), kind(a, "assignment").
.decl pt_sbinds(s: node, x: symbol, st: node)
pt_sbinds(s, x, st) :- pt_defn(s, x, f), pt_defstmt(f, st), pt_stmt(st, s).
pt_sbinds(s, x, st) :- pt_asg(s, x, _, a), pt_asgstmt(a, st), pt_stmt(st, s).
// An `@overload` def does not replace an earlier one: a stub's overloads are all the name's (their union is its
// type), and a later def that is not an overload (the implementation) replaces them all. Read from the decorator's
// own name, not its import: what a name is depends on what is live, which depends on this.
.decl pt_ovlstmt(st: node)
pt_ovlstmt(st) :- kind(st, "decorated_definition"), child(st, dc, _), kind(dc, "decorator"), child(dc, e, 0), text(e, "overload").
pt_ovlstmt(st) :- kind(st, "decorated_definition"), child(st, dc, _), kind(dc, "decorator"), child(dc, e, 0), kind(e, "attribute"),
    field(e, "attribute", a), text(a, "overload").
.decl pt_shadowed(st: node)
pt_shadowed(st) :- pt_sbinds(s, x, st), pt_sbinds(s, x, st2), st2 > st, !pt_ovlstmt(st2).
pt_shadowed(st) :- pt_sbinds(s, x, st), pt_sbinds(s, x, st2), st2 > st, !pt_ovlstmt(st).
.decl pt_live_def(s: node, x: symbol, f: node)
pt_live_def(s, x, f) :- pt_defn(s, x, f), pt_defstmt(f, st), !pt_shadowed(st).
.decl pt_live_asg(s: node, x: symbol, r: node)
pt_live_asg(s, x, r) :- pt_asg(s, x, r, a), !pt_asgstmt(a, _).
pt_live_asg(s, x, r) :- pt_asg(s, x, r, a), pt_asgstmt(a, st), !pt_shadowed(st).

// ---- decorators ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.decl pt_dexpr(f: node, e: node)
pt_dexpr(f, e) :- kind(dd, "decorated_definition"), field(dd, "definition", f), child(dd, dc, _), kind(dc, "decorator"), child(dc, e, 0).
.decl pt_transparent_q(q: symbol)
pt_transparent_q("abc.abstractmethod"). pt_transparent_q("typing.final"). pt_transparent_q("typing.override").
pt_transparent_q("typing.no_type_check"). pt_transparent_q("typing_extensions.final"). pt_transparent_q("typing_extensions.override").
pt_transparent_q("functools.wraps"). pt_transparent_q("functools.total_ordering"). pt_transparent_q("dataclasses.dataclass").
// The decorators stubs use (t21 §2.4): each gives back what it decorates, as a type checker reads it.
pt_transparent_q("typing.overload"). pt_transparent_q("typing_extensions.overload"). pt_transparent_q("typing.type_check_only").
pt_transparent_q("typing_extensions.deprecated"). pt_transparent_q("warnings.deprecated"). pt_transparent_q("typing.runtime_checkable").
pt_transparent_q("typing_extensions.runtime_checkable"). pt_transparent_q("typing_extensions.type_check_only").
pt_transparent_q("typing_extensions.disjoint_base"). pt_transparent_q("typing.disjoint_base").
.decl pt_transparent(e: node)
pt_transparent(e) :- pt_qn(e, q), pt_transparent_q(q).
pt_transparent(e) :- kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", g), pt_qn(g, q), pt_transparent_q(q).
// One defined in the module that uses it (typing.pyi's own `@overload`), by its qualified name: syntactic, as what
// a name is depends on the decorators.
// pt_ownq(e, q): identifier e, as a name of its own module (`typing.overload` in typing.pyi).
.decl pt_ownq(e: node, q: symbol)
pt_ownq(e, q) :- kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, x), docof(e, d), doc(d, _, m), q = @dot(m, x).
pt_transparent(e) :- pt_ownq(e, q), pt_transparent_q(q).
pt_transparent(e) :- pt_builtin_ref(e, "staticmethod").
pt_transparent(e) :- pt_builtin_ref(e, "classmethod").
.decl pt_opaque_dec(f: node, e: node)
pt_opaque_dec(f, e) :- pt_dexpr(f, e), !pt_transparent(e).
.decl pt_isstatic(f: node)
pt_isstatic(f) :- pt_dexpr(f, e), pt_builtin_ref(e, "staticmethod").
.decl pt_classmeth(f: node)
pt_classmeth(f) :- pt_dexpr(f, e), pt_builtin_ref(e, "classmethod").
.decl pt_nopaque(f: node, k: number)
pt_nopaque(f, k) :- pt_opaque_dec(f, _), k = count : { pt_opaque_dec(f, _) }.
// The one decorator that replaces the definition, when there is exactly one.
.decl pt_dec1(f: node, e: node)
pt_dec1(f, e) :- pt_nopaque(f, 1), pt_opaque_dec(f, e).
// A def whose every decorator not transparent is imported from outside the run, and is not one a library declares
// (`@retry(3)` of a library without stubs; a declared one, `contextmanager`, is `pt_ldec_known`'s), is still the code
// a call of its name runs, as far as the program can tell: such a decorator wraps the def and calls it, or gives it
// back. Its name holds `dfn` f: a call of it targets f, and is open (`pt_bopen`), for the wrapper is code the program
// does not read. A decorator that replaces the def by a value whose call does not run it (a `…property`,
// `functools.cached_property`) keeps the name unknown, with no target. (main's #875, on calls.rerail's program.)
// pt_dpart(e, p): p is decorator expression e or a part of its head (`functools.lru_cache` and `functools` of
// `functools.lru_cache(maxsize=None)`).
.decl pt_dpart(e: node, p: node)
pt_dpart(e, e) :- pt_dexpr(_, e).
pt_dpart(e, o) :- pt_dpart(e, p), kind(p, "attribute"), field(p, "object", o).
pt_dpart(e, g) :- pt_dpart(e, p), kind(p, "call"), field(p, "function", g).
// pt_dleaf(e, x): the last name of decorator e, or of the function a decorator call calls (`lru_cache`, `setter`).
.decl pt_dleaf(e: node, x: symbol)
pt_dleaf(e, x) :- pt_dexpr(_, e), kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, x).
pt_dleaf(e, x) :- pt_dexpr(_, e), pt_attr_of(e, _, x).
pt_dleaf(e, x) :- pt_dexpr(_, e), kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", g), kind(g, "identifier"), text(g, x).
pt_dleaf(e, x) :- pt_dexpr(_, e), kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", g), pt_attr_of(g, _, x).
.decl pt_replacing_dec(e: node)
pt_replacing_dec(e) :- pt_dleaf(e, x), suffix("property", x).
.decl pt_outside_dec(e: node)
pt_outside_dec(e) :- pt_dpart(e, h), pt_nameref(h, x), pt_look(h, x, s), pt_ext_import(s, x), !pt_run_import(s, x),
    !pt_rasg(s, x, _, _), !pt_rdefn(s, x, _), !pt_replacing_dec(e).
// pt_run_import(s, x): scope s imports x from a module of the run too (`try: from lib import x` / `except ImportError:
// from .compat import x`): the decorator may be the run's, read through `pt_decfn`.
.decl pt_run_import(s: node, x: symbol)
pt_run_import(s, x) :- pt_rifrom(s, x, m, _), pt_wsmod(m).
pt_run_import(s, x) :- pt_ribind(s, x, q), !pt_rifrom(s, x, _, _), pt_wsmod(q).
// pt_inner_dec(f): f has a decorator neither transparent nor from outside the run.
.decl pt_inner_dec(f: node)
pt_inner_dec(f) :- pt_opaque_dec(f, e), !pt_outside_dec(e).

// ---- functions: returns, returned parameters ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.decl pt_isasync(f: node)
pt_isasync(f) :- op(f, "async").
.decl pt_isgen(f: node)
pt_isgen(f) :- kind(y, "yield"), nearest(y, f, pt_fscope), kind(f, "function_definition").
.decl pt_retval(f: node, r: node)
pt_retval(f, r) :- kind(rs, "return_statement"), nearest(rs, f, pt_fscope), kind(f, "function_definition"), child(rs, r, 0).
// A return of the function's own parameter i (`return func`): the call's value is its i-th argument's.
.decl pt_retparam(f: node, i: number, r: node)
pt_retparam(f, i, r) :- pt_retval(f, r), pt_look(r, x, f), pt_param(f, x, i).
.decl pt_posarg(c: node, i: number, a: node)
pt_posarg(c, i, a) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "arguments", as), kind(as, "argument_list"), child(as, a, i), !kind(a, "keyword_argument"),
    !kind(a, "list_splat"), !kind(a, "dictionary_splat").
.decl pt_method(f: node, c: node)
pt_method(f, c) :- kind(f, "function_definition"), nearest(f, c, pt_scope), kind(c, "class_definition").

// ---- classes ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.decl pt_basex(c: node, e: node)
pt_basex(c, e) :- kind(c, "class_definition"), field(c, "superclasses", al), child(al, e, _), !kind(e, "keyword_argument").
.decl pt_base(c: node, b: node)
pt_base(c, b) :- pt_basex(c, e), pt_pv(e, "cls", b), !pt_special_base(e).
// The class and every workspace subclass: what a late-bound `self` or `cls` may be.
// The attribute lookups the program makes: a class and the attribute read from it (or from a `super()`).
.decl pt_asks(n: node, c: node, a: symbol)
pt_asks(n, c, a) :- pt_alook(n, c, a).
pt_asks(k, c, "__init__") :- pt_callee(k, e), pt_pv(e, "cls", c).
pt_asks(k, c, "__call__") :- pt_callee(k, e), pt_pv(e, "inst", c).
// need_name(a): an attribute name some lookup reads. Every reader of `found` asks with a name of need_attr's or
// alook's, or with __init__, __call__ or __new__.
// Attribute lookup: the class itself, else its bases (union over bases for multiple inheritance), for the names
// lookups read only: a stub's class binds many names no code reads.
.decl pt_found(c: node, a: symbol, at: node)
pt_found(c, a, c) :- pt_bound_in(c, a).
pt_found(c, a, x) :- pt_base(c, b), !pt_bound_in(c, a), pt_found(b, a, x).
.decl pt_anc(c: node, b: node)
pt_anc(c, c) :- kind(c, "class_definition").
pt_anc(c, b) :- pt_anc(c, m), pt_base(m, b).

// ---- declared types (annotations) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// A parameter's, a return's and a class attribute's annotation declare the values they hold. They are trusted, as a
// type checker trusts them: an annotation naming a workspace class C holds an instance of C or of any workspace
// subclass (the closed world `self` already assumes), a builtin class's name a value of it, `None` None. Unions
// (`A | B`, `Optional[A]`, `Union[A, B]`) are their members; a generic (`LazyResult[T]`, `list[int]`) is its class,
// without arguments; `type[C]` is C's class objects; `Self` is the method's class. Any other member (a type
// variable, `Any`, a `Protocol`, an external class) leaves the declaration open: its known members are a lower
// bound. A quoted annotation (`x: "Node"`, `list["Node"]`) is its code, parsed as an annotation (decision 0055).
.decl pt_ann(t: node, e: node)
pt_ann(t, e) :- kind(t, "type"), child(t, e, 0).
// pt_qann(s, e): string s is an annotation's whole expression, and e is its code's expression: the fragment
// "annotation" is rooted at a `type`, as tree-sitter writes an annotation (decision 0466), whose child is the
// expression (T's shape rooted it at a module of one statement, `(…)`; before 0466 the root was the expression).
// pt_qstr(s): string s is an annotation's whole expression, quoted, with a tree (python/annotation's ann_parse).
.decl pt_qstr(s: node)
pt_qstr(s) :- kind(t, "type"), child(t, s, 0), kind(s, "string"), ann_parse(s, _).
.decl pt_qann(s: node, e: node)
pt_qann(s, e) :- pt_qstr(s), ann_parse(s, r),
    (kind(r, "type"), child(r, e, 0) ; !kind(r, "type"), e = r).
.decl pt_union_q(q: symbol)
pt_union_q("typing.Optional"). pt_union_q("typing.Union"). pt_union_q("typing_extensions.Optional"). pt_union_q("typing_extensions.Union").
.decl pt_uhead(e: node)
pt_uhead(e) :- kind(e, "generic_type"), child(e, h, 0), pt_qn(h, q), pt_union_q(q).
pt_uhead(e) :- kind(e, "subscript"), field(e, "value", h), pt_qn(h, q), pt_union_q(q).
// pt_amem(t, e): e is a member of annotation t's union, or an expression that has members.
.decl pt_amem(t: node, e: node)
pt_amem(t, e) :- pt_ann(t, e).
pt_amem(t, m) :- pt_amem(t, e), kind(e, "binary_operator"), op(e, "|"), field(e, "left", m).
pt_amem(t, m) :- pt_amem(t, e), kind(e, "binary_operator"), op(e, "|"), field(e, "right", m).
pt_amem(t, m) :- pt_amem(t, e), kind(e, "parenthesized_expression"), child(e, m, 0).
pt_amem(t, r) :- pt_amem(t, s), host_node(s, _), pt_qann(s, r).   // a string nested in a quoted annotation's code
pt_amem(t, m) :- pt_amem(t, e), kind(e, "union_type"), child(e, u, _), child(u, m, 0).
pt_amem(t, m) :- pt_amem(t, e), pt_uhead(e), kind(e, "generic_type"), child(e, p, 1), child(p, u, _), child(u, m, 0).
pt_amem(t, m) :- pt_amem(t, e), pt_uhead(e), kind(e, "subscript"), field(e, "subscript", m).
.decl pt_asplit(e: node)
pt_asplit(e) :- kind(e, "binary_operator"), op(e, "|").
pt_asplit(e) :- kind(e, "parenthesized_expression").
pt_asplit(s) :- pt_qstr(s).
pt_asplit(e) :- kind(e, "union_type").
pt_asplit(e) :- pt_uhead(e).
// A member that is not split further, and the name it is headed by (`LazyResult` in `LazyResult[T]`).
.decl pt_aleaf(t: node, m: node)
pt_aleaf(t, m) :- pt_amem(t, m), !pt_asplit(m).
pt_aleaf(t, m) :- pt_amem(t, m), kind(m, "binary_operator"), !op(m, "|").
.decl pt_ahead(m: node, h: node)
pt_ahead(m, h) :- pt_aleaf(_, m), kind(m, "generic_type"), child(m, h, 0).
pt_ahead(m, h) :- pt_aleaf(_, m), kind(m, "subscript"), field(m, "value", h).
pt_ahead(m, m) :- pt_aleaf(_, m), !kind(m, "generic_type"), !kind(m, "subscript").
// The argument of a one-argument generic (`C` in `type[C]`).
.decl pt_aarg(m: node, a: node)
pt_aarg(m, a) :- kind(m, "generic_type"), child(m, p, 1), child(p, u, 0), !child(p, _, 1), child(u, a, 0).
pt_aarg(m, a) :- kind(m, "subscript"), field(m, "subscript", a), !kind(a, "expression_list"), !kind(a, "tuple").
// pt_ainst(t, c): t declares instances of class c (and of its workspace subclasses); pt_acls(t, c): c's class objects.
.decl pt_ainst(t: node, c: node)
pt_ainst(t, c) :- pt_aleaf(t, m), pt_ahead(m, h), pt_pv(h, "cls", c).
.decl pt_acls(t: node, c: node)
pt_acls(t, c) :- pt_aleaf(t, m), pt_ahead(m, h), pt_builtin_ref(h, "type"), pt_aarg(m, a), pt_pv(a, "cls", c).
// pt_aself(m): `Self`.
.decl pt_aself(m: node)
pt_aself(m) :- pt_aleaf(_, m), pt_ahead(m, h), pt_qn(h, "typing.Self").
pt_aself(m) :- pt_aleaf(_, m), pt_ahead(m, h), pt_qn(h, "typing_extensions.Self").
// pt_dtype(m, t): member m declares a value of builtin class t, or None.
.decl pt_dtype(m: node, t: symbol)
pt_dtype(m, "None") :- pt_aleaf(_, m), kind(m, "none").
pt_dtype(m, x) :- pt_aleaf(_, m), pt_ahead(m, h), pt_builtin_ref(h, x), pt_bclass(x), x != "object".
// A class whose instances need not derive from it: a `Protocol`.
.decl pt_proto_q(q: symbol)
pt_proto_q("typing.Protocol"). pt_proto_q("typing_extensions.Protocol").
.decl pt_aproto(c: node)
// A protocol lists `Protocol` among its own bases (PEP 544): a class deriving from a protocol is an ordinary class
// (`pathlib.Path` from `os.PathLike[str]`).
pt_aproto(c) :- pt_basex(c, e), pt_qn(e, q), pt_proto_q(q).
pt_aproto(c) :- pt_basex(c, e), kind(e, "generic_type"), child(e, h, 0), pt_qn(h, q), pt_proto_q(q).
pt_aproto(c) :- pt_basex(c, e), kind(e, "subscript"), field(e, "value", h), pt_qn(h, q), pt_proto_q(q).
.decl pt_aknown(t: node, m: node)
pt_aknown(t, m) :- pt_aleaf(t, m), pt_dtype(m, _).
pt_aknown(t, m) :- pt_aleaf(t, m), pt_aself(m).
pt_aknown(t, m) :- pt_aleaf(t, m), pt_ahead(m, h), pt_pv(h, "cls", c), !pt_aproto(c), !pt_builtin_ref(h, "type").
pt_aknown(t, m) :- pt_aleaf(t, m), pt_ahead(m, h), pt_builtin_ref(h, "type"), pt_aarg(m, a), pt_pv(a, "cls", _).
pt_aknown(t, m) :- pt_aleaf(t, m), pt_ahead(m, h), pt_lv(h, "cls", c), !pt_lproto(c), !pt_builtin_ref(h, "type").
pt_aknown(t, m) :- pt_aleaf(t, m), pt_ahead(m, h), pt_builtin_ref(h, "type"), pt_aarg(m, a), pt_lv(a, "cls", _).
.decl pt_aopen(t: node)
pt_aopen(t) :- pt_aleaf(t, m), !pt_aknown(t, m).
// A quoted annotation (`x: "Node"`) is its code's members: the annotation context's leaves of the string's tree, and
// what the context finds of each: its head, a `type[C]`'s argument, a builtin's or None's type, `Self`, and its names'
// lookups and qualified names, which the host's bindings give values (rule 5 of decision 0597).
pt_aleaf(t, m) :- pt_amem(t, s), pt_qstr(s), ann_parse(s, r), pt_q_aleaf(r, m).
pt_ahead(m, h) :- pt_q_ahead(m, h).
pt_aarg(m, a) :- pt_q_aarg(m, a).
pt_dtype(m, x) :- pt_q_dtype(m, x).
pt_aself(m) :- pt_q_aself(m).
pt_look(n, x, s) :- pt_q_look(n, x, s).
pt_qn(n, q) :- pt_q_qn(n, q).
pt_builtin_ref(n, x) :- pt_q_builtin_ref(n, x).
.context annotation of python roots ann_tree exports pt_aleaf, pt_ahead, pt_aarg, pt_dtype, pt_aself, pt_look, pt_qn, pt_builtin_ref
.from python pt_hstart, pt_up, pt_bound_in, pt_ibind, pt_modnode, pt_star for annotation
.from annotation pt_aleaf as pt_q_aleaf, pt_ahead as pt_q_ahead, pt_aarg as pt_q_aarg, pt_dtype as pt_q_dtype, pt_aself as pt_q_aself, pt_look as pt_q_look, pt_qn as pt_q_qn, pt_builtin_ref as pt_q_builtin_ref
// Parameters: `x: T` and `x: T = v` (the default's own value is added as an assignment's is).
.decl pt_pann(f: node, x: symbol, t: node)
pt_pann(f, x, t) :- field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, _), kind(p, "typed_parameter"), child(p, id, 0), kind(id, "identifier"),
    text(id, x), field(p, "type", t).
pt_pann(f, x, t) :- field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, _), kind(p, "typed_default_parameter"), field(p, "name", id), text(id, x),
    field(p, "type", t).
.decl pt_pdefault(f: node, x: symbol, v: node)
pt_pdefault(f, x, v) :- field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, _), kind(p, "typed_default_parameter"), field(p, "name", id), text(id, x),
    field(p, "value", v).
.decl pt_pclosed(f: node, x: symbol)
pt_pclosed(f, x) :- pt_pann(f, x, t), !pt_aopen(t).
// A parameter's declared classes, with their subclasses, only where the parameter is read: a function scope's
// values are read through `look` alone, and a stub's parameters are never read.
.decl pt_pread(f: node, x: symbol)
pt_pread(f, x) :- pt_pann(f, x, _), pt_look(_, x, f).
// uinst: ainst cut to the annotations these rules read (a library's stubs annotate `str` thousands of times; a new
// subclass of it looks up only these).
.decl pt_uann(t: node)
pt_uann(t) :- pt_pann(f, x, t), pt_pread(f, x).
pt_uann(t) :- pt_cann(c, x, t), pt_cread(c, x).
.decl pt_uinst(t: node, c: node)
pt_uinst(t, c) :- pt_uann(t), pt_ainst(t, c).
pt_bv(f, x, "inst", s) :- pt_pann(f, x, t), pt_pread(f, x), pt_uinst(t, c), pt_anc(s, c).
pt_bv(f, x, "cls", s) :- pt_pann(f, x, t), pt_pread(f, x), pt_acls(t, c), pt_anc(s, c).
pt_bv(f, x, "inst", s) :- pt_pann(f, x, t), pt_pread(f, x), pt_aleaf(t, m), pt_aself(m), pt_method(f, c), pt_anc(s, c).
pt_bv(f, x, k, v) :- pt_pdefault(f, x, d), pt_pv(d, k, v).
pt_tbv(f, x, "decl", m) :- pt_pann(f, x, t), pt_aleaf(t, m), pt_dtype(m, _).
pt_tbv(f, x, k, v) :- pt_pdefault(f, x, d), pt_tv(d, k, v).
// Returns: `def f(...) -> T`. A call of f holds T's values (beside what its returns are seen to hold); when T is
// closed, the call is known whatever its returns are.
.decl pt_rann(f: node, t: node)
pt_rann(f, t) :- kind(f, "function_definition"), field(f, "return_type", t).
.decl pt_rclosed(f: node)
pt_rclosed(f) :- pt_rann(f, t), !pt_aopen(t), !pt_isasync(f).
// pt_rret(f, "inst", k): f is declared to return an instance of class k (or of a subclass); "cls" for `type[k]`.
.decl pt_rret(f: node, w: symbol, k: node)
pt_rret(f, "inst", k) :- pt_rann(f, t), !pt_isasync(f), pt_ainst(t, k).
pt_rret(f, "cls", k) :- pt_rann(f, t), !pt_isasync(f), pt_acls(t, k).
pt_rret(f, "inst", k) :- pt_rann(f, t), !pt_isasync(f), pt_aleaf(t, m), pt_aself(m), pt_method(f, k).
// pt_cret(c, w, k): call c's declared return class. Joined with the subclasses last, so a new subclass row reaches
// only the calls declared to return its base.
.decl pt_cret(c: node, w: symbol, k: node)
pt_cret(c, w, k) :- pt_cfn(c, e, f), pt_rret(f, w, k), !pt_rgen(f, _).
pt_pv(c, w, s) :- pt_cret(c, w, k), pt_anc(s, k).
// pt_awaitf(w, c, f): `await c`, where call c runs the async def f (not an async generator, which is not awaited). Its
// value is what f returns, declared (`async def f() -> K`: the coroutine's result, not the call's) or returned.
.decl pt_awaitf(w: node, c: node, f: node)
pt_awaitf(w, c, f) :- kind(w, "await"), child(w, c, 0), pt_cfn(c, _, f), pt_isasync(f), !pt_isgen(f).
.decl pt_aclosed(f: node)
pt_aclosed(f) :- pt_rann(f, t), !pt_aopen(t), pt_isasync(f).
.decl pt_aret(f: node, w: symbol, k: node)
pt_aret(f, "inst", k) :- pt_rann(f, t), pt_isasync(f), pt_ainst(t, k).
pt_aret(f, "cls", k) :- pt_rann(f, t), pt_isasync(f), pt_acls(t, k).
pt_cret(w, k, c) :- pt_awaitf(w, _, f), pt_aret(f, k, c).
pt_pv(w, k, v) :- pt_awaitf(w, _, f), pt_fret(f, k, v).

// ---- generics (t21 §5.1, first version) --------------------------------------------------------------------------
// A class's type parameters, by position: `Generic[K, V]` (or `Protocol[T]`) among its bases, else the type variables
// its first generic base is given (`class list(MutableSequence[_T])`). A type variable: a module's `x = TypeVar(...)`.
.decl pt_tvarq(m: node, x: symbol)
pt_tvarq(m, x) :- pt_rasg(m, x, r, _), kind(m, "module"), kind(r, "call"), field(r, "function", e), text(e, "TypeVar").
pt_tvarq(m, x) :- pt_rasg(m, x, r, _), kind(m, "module"), kind(r, "call"), field(r, "function", e), field(e, "attribute", a), text(a, "TypeVar").
// pt_sarg(e, j, a): a is the j-th argument of the generic e (`dict[str, int]` as a subscript or an annotation's type).
// pt_pred(i, j): j = i - 1, for the positions a generic's arguments and a method's parameters take.
.decl pt_pred(i: number, j: number)
pt_pred(1, 0). pt_pred(2, 1). pt_pred(3, 2). pt_pred(4, 3). pt_pred(5, 4). pt_pred(6, 5). pt_pred(7, 6). pt_pred(8, 7).
.decl pt_sarg(e: node, j: number, a: node)
pt_sarg(e, j, a) :- kind(e, "subscript"), child(e, a, i), pt_pred(i, j).
pt_sarg(e, j, a) :- kind(e, "generic_type"), child(e, p, 1), kind(p, "type_parameter"), child(p, u, j), child(u, a, 0).
// Read from the bases as written, not their values (which read these): `Generic[...]` and `Protocol[...]` by name.
.decl pt_pform(e: node)
pt_pform(e) :- kind(e, "subscript"), field(e, "value", h), kind(h, "identifier"), text(h, x), pt_pform_name(x).
pt_pform(e) :- kind(e, "subscript"), field(e, "value", h), field(h, "attribute", a), text(a, x), pt_pform_name(x).
.decl pt_pform_name(x: symbol)
pt_pform_name("Generic"). pt_pform_name("Protocol").
.decl pt_explicit_params(c: node)
pt_explicit_params(c) :- pt_basex(c, e), pt_pform(e).
.decl pt_gbase_at(c: node, e: node, j: number)
pt_gbase_at(c, e, j) :- field(c, "superclasses", al), child(al, e, j), kind(e, "subscript"), !pt_pform(e), pt_sarg(e, _, a),
    kind(a, "identifier"), text(a, y), nearest(c, m, pt_scope), pt_tvarq(m, y).
.decl pt_gbase_later(c: node, j: number)
pt_gbase_later(c, j) :- pt_gbase_at(c, _, j), pt_gbase_at(c, _, i), i < j.
.decl pt_cparam(c: node, i: number, y: symbol)
pt_cparam(c, i, y) :- pt_basex(c, e), pt_pform(e), pt_sarg(e, i, a), kind(a, "identifier"), text(a, y).
// Else the type variables of its first base with one as an argument (`_GeneratorContextManager`'s first base takes
// `Generator[_T_co, ...]`, not a type variable).
pt_cparam(c, i, y) :- pt_gbase_at(c, e, j), !pt_gbase_later(c, j), !pt_explicit_params(c), pt_sarg(e, i, a), kind(a, "identifier"), text(a, y),
    nearest(c, m, pt_scope), pt_tvarq(m, y).
// pt_tmap(k, i, a, y): ancestor a's parameter y is k's parameter i; pt_tfix(k, a, y, x): it is the annotation x, fixed by
// k's bases (`class D(M[str, int])`).
.decl pt_tmap(k: node, i: number, a: node, y: symbol)
pt_tmap(k, i, k, y) :- pt_cparam(k, i, y).
pt_tmap(k, i, a, y) :- pt_basex(k, b), pt_gbase(b, bc), pt_sarg(b, j, x), kind(x, "identifier"), text(x, z), pt_cparam(k, i, z), pt_tmap(bc, j, a, y).
.decl pt_tparg(k: node, x: node)
pt_tparg(k, x) :- pt_basex(k, b), pt_sarg(b, _, x), kind(x, "identifier"), text(x, z), pt_cparam(k, _, z).
.decl pt_tfix(k: node, a: node, y: symbol, x: node)
pt_tfix(k, a, y, x) :- pt_basex(k, b), pt_gbase(b, bc), pt_sarg(b, j, x), !pt_tparg(k, x), pt_tmap(bc, j, a, y).
pt_tfix(k, a, y, x) :- pt_base(k, bc), pt_tfix(bc, a, y, x).
// A generic annotation's value: the annotation itself (`dict[str, int]`), beside its class's instances, so a method
// declared to return the class's parameter returns what the annotation gives it.
.decl pt_gleaf(t: node, m: node)
pt_gleaf(t, m) :- pt_uann(t), pt_aleaf(t, m), pt_ahead(m, h), m != h, pt_pv(h, "cls", k), pt_cparam(k, _, _).
pt_bv(f, x, "gen", m) :- pt_pann(f, x, t), pt_pread(f, x), pt_gleaf(t, m).
pt_bv(c, x, "gen", m) :- pt_cann(c, x, t), pt_cread(c, x), pt_gleaf(t, m).
// pt_rtvar(f, a, y): method f of class a is declared to return a's parameter y; pt_rpvar(f, i, y): function f returns its
// own type variable y, which its parameter i is declared to be (`def get(self, key, default: _T) -> _VT | _T`).
.decl pt_rtvar(f: node, a: node, y: symbol)
pt_rtvar(f, a, y) :- pt_rann(f, t), !pt_isasync(f), pt_aleaf(t, r), kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, y), pt_method(f, a), pt_cparam(a, _, y).
.decl pt_rpvar(f: node, i: number, y: symbol)
pt_rpvar(f, i, y) :- pt_rann(f, t), !pt_isasync(f), pt_aleaf(t, r), kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, y), pt_pann(f, x, pt), pt_aleaf(pt, pr),
    kind(pr, "identifier"), text(pr, y), pt_param(f, x, i), !pt_rtvar(f, _, y).
// pt_rgen(f, r): f is declared to return the generic r (`-> Iterator[_T]`, `-> dict[str, V]`), a class's subscript, not a
// special form's (`Optional[...]`, `type[...]`, `Callable[...]`). Read as written, so the recursion can tell its
// calls apart.
.decl pt_rgen(f: node, r: node)
pt_rgen(f, r) :- pt_rann(f, t), pt_ann(t, r), !pt_isasync(f), kind(r, "generic_type"), child(r, h, 0), pt_gname(h, x), !pt_gform_name(x).
pt_rgen(f, r) :- pt_rann(f, t), pt_ann(t, r), !pt_isasync(f), kind(r, "subscript"), field(r, "value", h), pt_gname(h, x), !pt_gform_name(x).
.decl pt_gname(h: node, x: symbol)
pt_gname(h, x) :- kind(h, "identifier"), text(h, x).
pt_gname(h, x) :- kind(h, "attribute"), field(h, "attribute", a), text(a, x).
.decl pt_gform_name(x: symbol)
pt_gform_name("Optional"). pt_gform_name("Union"). pt_gform_name("type"). pt_gform_name("Type"). pt_gform_name("Callable"). pt_gform_name("Literal").
pt_gform_name("Annotated"). pt_gform_name("ClassVar"). pt_gform_name("Final"). pt_gform_name("TypeGuard"). pt_gform_name("TypeIs").
pt_gform_name("Concatenate"). pt_gform_name("Unpack"). pt_gform_name("Required"). pt_gform_name("NotRequired"). pt_gform_name("ReadOnly").
// pt_tvar_of(f, z): argument z of f's declared generic is a parameter of f's class.
.decl pt_tvar_of(f: node, z: node)
pt_tvar_of(f, z) :- pt_rgen(f, r), pt_method(f, a), pt_sarg(r, _, z), kind(z, "identifier"), text(z, y), pt_cparam(a, _, y).
// pt_gfn(c, f): call c (a call, an implicit call) runs f, declared to return its class's parameter or a generic;
// pt_gcall(c, o, f): on o's value.
.decl pt_gret(f: node)
pt_gret(f) :- pt_rtvar(f, _, _).
pt_gret(f) :- pt_rgen(f, _).
.decl pt_gfn(c: node, f: node)
pt_gfn(c, f) :- pt_cfn(c, e, f), pt_gret(f).
pt_gfn(c, f) :- pt_ifn(c, f), pt_gret(f).
.decl pt_gcall(c: node, o: node, f: node)
pt_gcall(c, o, f) :- pt_gfn(c, f), pt_callee(c, n), pt_attr_of(n, o, _).
pt_gcall(c, o, f) :- pt_gfn(c, f), pt_icall(c, o, _).
// A generic value's class and arguments: an annotation's as written (`dict[str, V]`), or a call's declared generic
// return, its type variables bound at the call (`list[V]`'s `__iter__() -> Iterator[_T]` is an Iterator of V). The
// call's node stands for the generic it returns. Its class is exactly the declared one: a subclass's method is
// typed by it.
.decl pt_ghcls(v: node, k: node)
pt_ghcls(m, k) :- pt_gleaf(_, m), pt_ahead(m, h), pt_pv(h, "cls", k).
pt_ghcls(x, k) :- pt_sarg(_, _, x), pt_ghead(x, h), x != h, pt_pv(h, "cls", k), pt_cparam(k, _, _).
pt_ghcls(c, k) :- pt_gfn(c, f), pt_rgen(f, r), pt_ahead(r, h), pt_pv(h, "cls", k).
.decl pt_garg(v: node, i: number, x: node)
pt_garg(m, i, x) :- pt_ghcls(m, _), pt_sarg(m, i, x).
pt_garg(c, j, x) :- pt_gcall(c, _, f), pt_rgen(f, r), pt_sarg(r, j, z), pt_tvar_of(f, z), text(z, y), pt_method(f, a), pt_gpar(c, a, y, x).
pt_garg(c, j, z) :- pt_gfn(c, f), pt_rgen(f, r), pt_sarg(r, j, z), !pt_tvar_of(f, z).
pt_pv(c, "gen", c) :- pt_gfn(c, f), pt_rgen(f, _), pt_ghcls(c, _).
pt_pv(c, "inst", k) :- pt_gfn(c, f), pt_rgen(f, _), pt_ghcls(c, k).
// A wrapper's call (`wrap`) holds the B its decorator g declares, exactly; B's type variables are bound by matching A
// against f's declared return (`Generator[None, None, None]` against `Iterator[_T_co]`, through Generator's bases).
.decl pt_wcall(c: node, f: node, g: node)
pt_wcall(c, f, g) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "wfn", f), pt_decfn(f, g).
pt_ghcls(c, k) :- pt_wcall(c, _, g), pt_wrap(g, _, b), pt_gann_head(b, h), pt_pv(h, "cls", k).
pt_pv(c, "inst", k) :- pt_wcall(c, _, g), pt_wrap(g, _, b), pt_gann_head(b, h), pt_pv(h, "cls", k).
pt_pv(c, "gen", c) :- pt_wcall(c, _, _), pt_ghcls(c, _).
pt_garg(c, j, x) :- pt_wcall(c, f, g), pt_wrap(g, _, b), pt_sarg(b, j, z), kind(z, "identifier"), text(z, y), pt_wbind(f, g, y, x).
// pt_wbind(f, g, y, x): A's argument i is g's type variable y, and f's declared return rf, whose class kf has A's class
// ka among its ancestors, gives ka's parameter i the annotation x.
.decl pt_wbind(f: node, g: node, y: symbol, x: node)
pt_wbind(f, g, y, x) :- pt_decfn(f, g), pt_wrap(g, a, _), pt_gann_head(a, ha), pt_pv(ha, "cls", ka), pt_sarg(a, i, z), kind(z, "identifier"), text(z, y),
    pt_cparam(ka, i, w), pt_rann(f, t), pt_ann(t, rf), pt_gann_head(rf, hf), pt_pv(hf, "cls", kf), pt_tmap(kf, i2, ka, w), pt_sarg(rf, i2, x).
// pt_gpar(c, a, y, x): at call c, the receiver binds its class a's parameter y to the annotation x: through its generic
// value's arguments, or its class's bases (`class D(M[str, int])`).
.decl pt_gpar(c: node, a: node, y: symbol, x: node)
pt_gpar(c, a, y, x) :- pt_gcall(c, o, f), pt_method(f, a), pt_pv(o, "gen", g), pt_ghcls(g, k), pt_tmap(k, i, a, y), pt_garg(g, i, x).
pt_gpar(c, a, y, x) :- pt_gcall(c, o, f), pt_method(f, a), pt_pv(o, "inst", k), pt_tfix(k, a, y, x).
// pt_gbind(c, x): call c's value is what annotation x declares.
.decl pt_gbind(c: node, x: node)
pt_gbind(c, x) :- pt_gcall(c, _, f), pt_rtvar(f, a, y), pt_gpar(c, a, y, x).
.decl pt_ghead(x: node, h: node)
pt_ghead(x, h) :- pt_sarg(_, _, x), kind(x, "subscript"), field(x, "value", h).
pt_ghead(x, h) :- pt_sarg(_, _, x), kind(x, "generic_type"), child(x, h, 0).
pt_ghead(x, x) :- pt_sarg(_, _, x), !kind(x, "subscript"), !kind(x, "generic_type").
// The bound class first, joined with its subclasses last (as `cret`): a new subclass row then reaches only the calls
// bound to its base, not every class's value.
.decl pt_gcls(c: node, x: node, k: node)
pt_gcls(c, x, k) :- pt_gbind(c, x), pt_ghead(x, h), pt_pv(h, "cls", k).
pt_pv(c, "inst", s) :- pt_gcls(c, _, k), pt_anc(s, k).
pt_pv(c, "gen", x) :- pt_gcls(c, x, k), pt_ghead(x, h), x != h, pt_cparam(k, _, _).
// A function's own type variable, from the argument its parameter is given (a method's arguments follow `self`).
pt_pv(c, k, v) :- pt_cfn(c, e, f), !pt_method(f, _), pt_rpvar(f, i, _), pt_posarg(c, i, a), pt_pv(a, k, v).
pt_pv(c, k, v) :- pt_cfn(c, e, f), pt_attr_of(e, _, _), pt_method(f, _), pt_rpvar(f, i, _), pt_pred(i, j), pt_posarg(c, j, a), pt_pv(a, k, v).
// Or from the generic its parameter is declared (`sorted(iterable: Iterable[_T]) -> list[_T]`): pt_ownvar(f, y), f's
// return reads its own type variable y; pt_fgp(f, i, ka, w, y), f's parameter i is declared a generic of class ka whose
// parameter w is y; pt_fbind(c, f, y, x), at call c the argument's generic value, or its class's bases, give w the
// annotation x.
.decl pt_ownvar(f: node, y: symbol)
pt_ownvar(f, y) :- pt_rann(f, t), !pt_isasync(f), pt_aleaf(t, r), kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, y), !pt_method(f, _).
pt_ownvar(f, y) :- pt_rann(f, t), !pt_isasync(f), pt_aleaf(t, r), kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, y), pt_method(f, a), !pt_cparam(a, _, y).
pt_ownvar(f, y) :- pt_rgen(f, r), pt_sarg(r, _, z), kind(z, "identifier"), text(z, y), !pt_method(f, _).
pt_ownvar(f, y) :- pt_rgen(f, r), pt_sarg(r, _, z), kind(z, "identifier"), text(z, y), !pt_tvar_of(f, z), pt_method(f, _).
.decl pt_fgp(f: node, i: number, ka: node, w: symbol, y: symbol)
pt_fgp(f, i, ka, w, y) :- pt_ownvar(f, y), pt_pann(f, x, pt), pt_param(f, x, i), pt_ann(pt, g), pt_gann_head(g, h), pt_pv(h, "cls", ka), pt_sarg(g, j, z),
    kind(z, "identifier"), text(z, y), pt_cparam(ka, j, w).
.decl pt_fcall(c: node, f: node, i: number, a: node)
pt_fcall(c, f, i, a) :- pt_cfn(c, e, f), !pt_method(f, _), pt_fgp(f, i, _, _, _), pt_posarg(c, i, a).
pt_fcall(c, f, i, a) :- pt_cfn(c, e, f), pt_attr_of(e, _, _), pt_method(f, _), pt_fgp(f, i, _, _, _), pt_pred(i, j), pt_posarg(c, j, a).
.decl pt_fbind(c: node, f: node, y: symbol, x: node)
pt_fbind(c, f, y, x) :- pt_fcall(c, f, i, a), pt_fgp(f, i, ka, w, y), pt_pv(a, "gen", g), pt_ghcls(g, k), pt_tmap(k, i2, ka, w), pt_garg(g, i2, x).
pt_fbind(c, f, y, x) :- pt_fcall(c, f, i, a), pt_fgp(f, i, ka, w, y), pt_pv(a, "inst", k), pt_tfix(k, ka, w, x).
pt_gbind(c, x) :- pt_fbind(c, f, y, x), pt_rann(f, t), pt_aleaf(t, r), kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, y).
pt_garg(c, j, x) :- pt_fbind(c, f, y, x), pt_rgen(f, r), pt_sarg(r, j, z), kind(z, "identifier"), text(z, y).
// A protocol's parameter, which one of its methods is declared to return (`next(i: SupportsNext[_T]) -> _T`): f
// returns what the argument's method of that name returns, as an implicit call (`i.__next__()`) does. Not an `icall`,
// which is read before values (its receiver is a value root): pt_pfn(c, o, f), call c runs o's method f.
.decl pt_pmeth(ka: node, w: symbol, m: symbol)
pt_pmeth(ka, w, m) :- pt_rtvar(mm, ka, w), pt_aproto(ka), field(mm, "name", n), text(n, m).
.decl pt_pcall(c: node, o: node, m: symbol)
pt_pcall(c, a, m) :- pt_fcall(c, f, i, a), pt_fgp(f, i, ka, w, y), pt_pmeth(ka, w, m), pt_rann(f, t), pt_aleaf(t, r), kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, y).
pt_asks(c, k, m) :- pt_pcall(c, o, m), pt_pv(o, "inst", k).
.decl pt_pfn(c: node, o: node, f: node)
pt_pfn(c, o, f) :- pt_pcall(c, o, m), pt_pv(o, "inst", k), pt_fv(c, k, m, "fn", f).
pt_pv(c, k, v) :- pt_pfn(c, _, f), !pt_isasync(f), !pt_isgen(f), pt_fret(f, k, v).
pt_cret(c, w, k) :- pt_pfn(c, _, f), pt_rret(f, w, k), !pt_rgen(f, _).
pt_gfn(c, f) :- pt_pfn(c, _, f), pt_gret(f).
pt_gcall(c, o, f) :- pt_gfn(c, f), pt_pfn(c, o, f).

// ---- implicit calls -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// pt_icall(c, o, a): c's value is what o's method a returns, a call with no node for the method: a subscript `o[i]` is
// `o.__getitem__(i)`. A class's subscript (`list[int]`, a generic alias) is no call of it.
.decl pt_icall(c: node, o: node, a: symbol)
pt_icall(c, o, "__getitem__") :- pt_vpos(c), kind(c, "subscript"), field(c, "value", o).
// A loop's statement holds its iterator, its target the iterator's next value; a `with` alias the value entered.
pt_icall(a, it, "__iter__") :- pt_rasg(_, _, l, a), kind(a, "for_statement"), !op(a, "async"), field(a, "right", it).
pt_icall(l, a, "__next__") :- pt_rasg(_, _, l, a), kind(a, "for_statement"), !op(a, "async").
pt_icall(t, e, "__enter__") :- pt_rasg(_, _, t, a), kind(a, "with_statement"), !op(a, "async"), kind(t, "as_pattern_target"), field(p, "alias", t),
    child(p, e, 0).
// `async for`: the statement holds `it.__aiter__()`, a plain call; its target the awaited `__anext__()` of that.
pt_icall(a, it, "__aiter__") :- pt_rasg(_, _, l, a), kind(a, "for_statement"), op(a, "async"), field(a, "right", it).
// pt_iawait(c, o, a): c's value is the result of awaiting o's method a, an implicit call: an `async for` target's
// `__anext__()`, an `async with` alias's `__aenter__()`.
.decl pt_iawait(c: node, o: node, a: symbol)
pt_iawait(l, a, "__anext__") :- pt_rasg(_, _, l, a), kind(a, "for_statement"), op(a, "async").
pt_iawait(t, e, "__aenter__") :- pt_rasg(_, _, t, a), kind(a, "with_statement"), op(a, "async"), kind(t, "as_pattern_target"), field(p, "alias", t),
    child(p, e, 0).
pt_vroot(o) :- pt_iawait(_, o, _).
pt_asks(c, k, a) :- pt_iawait(c, o, a), pt_pv(o, "inst", k).
// pt_iafn(c, f): the workspace `async def` an awaited implicit call runs; c holds its coroutine's result, as `await`
// of a call does (`awaitf`).
.decl pt_iafn(c: node, f: node)
pt_iafn(c, f) :- pt_iawait(c, o, a), pt_pv(o, "inst", k), pt_fv(c, k, a, "fn", f), pt_isasync(f), !pt_isgen(f).
pt_cret(c, w, k) :- pt_iafn(c, f), pt_aret(f, w, k).
pt_pv(c, k, v) :- pt_iafn(c, f), pt_fret(f, k, v).
pt_vroot(o) :- pt_icall(_, o, _).
pt_asks(c, k, a) :- pt_icall(c, o, a), pt_pv(o, "inst", k).
// pt_ifn(c, f): the method an implicit call runs.
.decl pt_ifn(c: node, f: node)
pt_ifn(c, f) :- pt_icall(c, o, a), pt_pv(o, "inst", k), pt_fv(c, k, a, "fn", f).
pt_pv(c, k, v) :- pt_ifn(c, f), !pt_isasync(f), !pt_isgen(f), pt_fret(f, k, v).
pt_cret(c, w, k) :- pt_ifn(c, f), pt_rret(f, w, k), !pt_rgen(f, _).
pt_tv(c, "decl", m) :- pt_cfn(c, e, f), !pt_isasync(f), pt_rann(f, t), pt_aleaf(t, m), pt_dtype(m, _).
// Class attributes: `x: T` or `x: T = v` in a class body binds x there; T's values are what instances may read.
.decl pt_cann(c: node, x: symbol, t: node)
pt_cann(c, x, t) :- kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", l), kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, x), field(a, "type", t), nearest(a, c, pt_scope),
    kind(c, "class_definition"), !py_dead_at(a).
// `self.x: T` or `self.x: T = v` in a method declares the attribute on its class, as `x: T` in the body does (`self`:
// the method's first parameter; not `selfparam`, whose static test reads the decorators' values, which read this).
pt_cann(c, x, t) :- kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", l), kind(l, "attribute"), field(l, "object", o), kind(o, "identifier"),
    text(o, sn), field(l, "attribute", at), text(at, x), field(a, "type", t), nearest(a, f, pt_fdef), pt_method(f, c), pt_param(f, sn, 0),
    !py_dead_at(a).
pt_bound_in(c, x) :- pt_cann(c, x, _).
// A class attribute's, only where it is read: through `found` (a name a lookup reads), or by name in the class
// body (`look`).
.decl pt_cread(c: node, x: symbol)
pt_cread(c, x) :- pt_cann(c, x, _).
pt_cread(c, x) :- pt_cann(c, x, _), pt_look(_, x, c).
pt_bv(c, x, "inst", s) :- pt_cann(c, x, t), pt_cread(c, x), pt_uinst(t, k), pt_anc(s, k).
pt_bv(c, x, "cls", s) :- pt_cann(c, x, t), pt_cread(c, x), pt_acls(t, k), pt_anc(s, k).
pt_tbv(c, x, "decl", m) :- pt_cann(c, x, t), pt_aleaf(t, m), pt_dtype(m, _).
// An attribute declared closed: assignments elsewhere (`self.x = ...`) conform to it.
.decl pt_adeclared(c: node, a: symbol)
pt_adeclared(c, a) :- pt_found(c, a, at), pt_cann(at, a, t), !pt_aopen(t).
// A decorator declared to return its argument's own type (`def d(fn: F) -> F`, F a type variable: a type
// parameter of d, or a module's `TypeVar`): the decorated name keeps the function, as a type checker reads it.
.decl pt_tvar(g: node, x: symbol)
pt_tvar(g, x) :- field(g, "type_parameters", tp), child(tp, p, _), child(p, e, 0), pt_ann(p, e), kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, x).
pt_tvar(g, x) :- field(g, "type_parameters", tp), child(tp, p, _), child(p, e, 0), pt_ann(p, e), kind(e, "constrained_type"), child(e, u, 0),
    child(u, i, 0), kind(i, "identifier"), text(i, x).
// pt_mtvar(d, x): x is a module-level `TypeVar` of document d, in scope in each of its functions.
.decl pt_mtvar(m: node, x: symbol)
pt_mtvar(m, x) :- pt_modnode(_, m), pt_rasg(m, x, r, _), pt_callee(r, h), pt_qn(h, "typing.TypeVar").
.decl pt_ident_dec(g: node)
pt_ident_dec(g) :- pt_param(g, x, 0), pt_pann(g, x, t), pt_ann(t, e), kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, v), pt_rann(g, r), pt_ann(r, e2), kind(e2, "identifier"),
    text(e2, v), pt_tvar(g, v).
pt_ident_dec(g) :- pt_param(g, x, 0), pt_pann(g, x, t), pt_ann(t, e), kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, v), pt_rann(g, r), pt_ann(r, e2), kind(e2, "identifier"),
    text(e2, v), docof(g, d), pt_modnode(d, mm), pt_mtvar(mm, v).
// A class decorator's form, `(cls: type[T]) -> type[T]`.
pt_ident_dec(g) :- pt_param(g, x, 0), pt_pann(g, x, t), pt_ann(t, e), pt_typeof_var(e, v), pt_rann(g, r), pt_ann(r, e2), pt_typeof_var(e2, v), pt_tvar(g, v).
pt_ident_dec(g) :- pt_param(g, x, 0), pt_pann(g, x, t), pt_ann(t, e), pt_typeof_var(e, v), pt_rann(g, r), pt_ann(r, e2), pt_typeof_var(e2, v), docof(g, d), pt_modnode(d, mm), pt_mtvar(mm, v).
// pt_typeof_var(e, v): e is `type[v]` (or `Type[v]`), v a name.
.decl pt_typeof_var(e: node, v: symbol)
pt_typeof_var(e, v) :- kind(e, "generic_type"), child(e, h, 0), text(h, n), pt_type_form(n), pt_aarg(e, a), kind(a, "identifier"), text(a, v).
pt_typeof_var(e, v) :- kind(e, "subscript"), field(e, "value", h), text(h, n), pt_type_form(n), pt_aarg(e, a), kind(a, "identifier"), text(a, v).
.decl pt_type_form(n: symbol)
pt_type_form("type"). pt_type_form("Type").

// ---- values ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.decl pt_attr_of(n: node, o: node, a: symbol)
pt_attr_of(n, o, a) :- kind(n, "attribute"), field(n, "object", o), field(n, "attribute", at), text(at, a).
.decl pt_callee(c: node, e: node)
// A call in a guest (a quoted annotation's code) is not evaluated: only its names are read.
pt_callee(c, e) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", e), !host_node(c, _).
// Qualified names: an imported name and attributes of one (`os.path.join`), whether or not the workspace defines it.
.decl pt_qn(n: node, q: symbol)
pt_qn(n, q) :- pt_look(n, x, s), pt_ibind(s, x, q).
pt_qn(n, @dot(q, a)) :- pt_attr_of(n, o, a), pt_qn(o, q).
// What a workspace symbol denotes, by its symbol: a module, or a module-level binding of one (`m.x`). A reader in
// another document finds it by symbol only: the name it reads is resolved by P2 (`pt_lres`, through `types__binds`'
// imports and re-exports) to the symbol that binds it, and that symbol's binding (`pt_wkey`: `m.x#k`, x's k-th
// definition, is a binding of `m.x`) is looked up here. P3 follows no import across documents itself.
.decl pt_qv(m: node, q: symbol, k: symbol, v: node)
pt_qv(m, q, "mod", m) :- pt_modname(m, q).
pt_qv(m, @dot(q, x), k, v) :- pt_modname(m, q), pt_bv(m, x, k, v).
// pt_wkey(d, w): symbol d, as P2 names it, is workspace binding w of `qv`, `lqv`, `tqv`, `qopen`.
.decl pt_wkey(d: symbol, w: symbol)
pt_wkey(d, w) :- pt_lres(_, d), w = @replace_all(d, "#[0-9]+$", "").
pt_wkey(d, w) :- pt_starx(_, _, d), w = @replace_all(d, "#[0-9]+$", "").
// pt_wres(q, w): the name q a document reads is workspace binding w.
.decl pt_wres(q: symbol, w: symbol)
pt_wres(q, w) :- pt_lres(q, d), pt_wkey(d, w).
// `from n import *` at a module's top level: the module binds each name P2 binds it to that it does not bind itself
// (n's `__all__`, or its public names: `types__binds`), each to the symbol P2 resolves it to.
.decl pt_star_from(m: node, n: symbol)
pt_star_from(m, n) :- kind(i, "import_from_statement"), child(i, w, _), kind(w, "wildcard_import"), nearest(i, m, pt_scope),
    pt_modname(m, _), pt_impmod(i, n).
.decl pt_starx(m: node, x: symbol, d: symbol)
pt_starx(m, x, d) :- pt_star_from(m, _), pt_modname(m, q), types__binds(q, x, d), x != "*", !pt_rbound(m, x).
pt_bv(m, x, k, v) :- pt_starx(m, x, d), pt_wkey(d, w), pt_qv(_, w, k, v).

// Binding values: what name x of scope s may hold.
.decl pt_bv(s: node, x: symbol, k: symbol, v: node)
pt_bv(s, x, "fn", f) :- pt_live_def(s, x, f), kind(f, "function_definition"), !pt_opaque_dec(f, _).
// A def under decorators from outside the run (`pt_outside_dec`): its calls run it, and more the program does not read.
pt_bv(s, x, "dfn", f) :- pt_live_def(s, x, f), kind(f, "function_definition"), pt_opaque_dec(f, _), !pt_inner_dec(f).
pt_bv(s, x, "cls", c) :- pt_live_def(s, x, c), kind(c, "class_definition").
// pt_decfn(f, g): f's one decorator is function g; pt_decval(f, k, v): what g returns, f's value. Made first, so each
// join starts from the few decorated definitions, not from every expression that names g.
.decl pt_decfn(f: node, g: node)
pt_decfn(f, g) :- pt_dec1(f, e), pt_pv(e, "fn", g).
.decl pt_decval(f: node, k: symbol, v: node)
pt_decval(f, k, v) :- pt_decfn(f, g), !pt_ident_dec(g), pt_retval(g, r), pt_pv(r, k, v).
// A decorator that returns its argument keeps the definition, a function or a class.
.decl pt_defk(f: node, k: symbol)
pt_defk(f, "fn") :- kind(f, "function_definition").
pt_defk(f, "cls") :- kind(f, "class_definition").
pt_bv(s, x, k, f) :- pt_live_def(s, x, f), pt_decfn(f, g), pt_retparam(g, 0, _), pt_defk(f, k).
pt_bv(s, x, k, v) :- pt_live_def(s, x, f), pt_decval(f, k, v).
pt_bv(s, x, k, f) :- pt_live_def(s, x, f), pt_decfn(f, g), pt_ident_dec(g), pt_defk(f, k).
// A decorator declared `(f: Callable[P, A]) -> Callable[P, B]` (`contextlib.contextmanager`) gives back a wrapper of
// f's parameters: its value is `wfn` f, whose call runs f and holds a B (`wcall`).
.decl pt_wrap(g: node, a: node, b: node)
pt_wrap(g, a, b) :- pt_param(g, x, 0), pt_pann(g, x, t), pt_ann(t, ca), pt_callable_ann(ca, p, a), pt_rann(g, r), pt_ann(r, cb), pt_callable_ann(cb, p, b).
.decl pt_callable_ann(e: node, p: symbol, r: node)
pt_callable_ann(e, p, r) :- pt_gann_head(e, h), pt_gname(h, "Callable"), pt_sarg(e, 0, pe), kind(pe, "identifier"), text(pe, p), pt_sarg(e, 1, r).
// pt_gann_head(e, h): the generic annotation e is headed by h (`Iterator` in `Iterator[_T]`), read as written.
.decl pt_gann_head(e: node, h: node)
pt_gann_head(e, h) :- kind(e, "generic_type"), child(e, h, 0).
pt_gann_head(e, h) :- kind(e, "subscript"), field(e, "value", h).
pt_bv(s, x, "wfn", f) :- pt_live_def(s, x, f), pt_decfn(f, g), pt_wrap(g, _, _), !pt_ident_dec(g).
pt_bv(s, x, k, v) :- pt_live_asg(s, x, r), pt_pv(r, k, v).
pt_bv(s, x, k, v) :- pt_ibind(s, x, q), pt_wres(q, w), pt_qv(_, w, k, v).
// `self` (the first parameter of a method that is not static) and `cls` (of a class method) are late bound: the
// class and each of its workspace subclasses.
pt_bv(f, x, "inst", s) :- pt_method(f, c), pt_param(f, x, 0), !pt_isstatic(f), !pt_classmeth(f), pt_anc(s, c).
pt_bv(f, x, "cls", s) :- pt_method(f, c), pt_param(f, x, 0), pt_classmeth(f), pt_anc(s, c).

.decl pt_pv(n: node, k: symbol, v: node)
pt_pv(n, k, v) :- pt_look(n, x, s), pt_bv(s, x, k, v).
pt_pv(n, k, v) :- pt_qn(n, q), pt_wres(q, w), pt_qv(_, w, k, v).
pt_pv(n, k, v) :- pt_alook(n, c, a), pt_fv(n, c, a, k, v).
// pt_fv(c, a, k, v): attribute a of class c, where it is found (on c or a base), may hold a k v.
.decl pt_fv(n: node, c: node, a: symbol, k: symbol, v: node)
pt_fv(n, c, a, k, v) :- pt_asks(n, c, a), pt_found(c, a, at), pt_bv(at, a, k, v).
// pt_alook(n, c, a): the attribute `o.a` at n is looked up on class c: o's class, o itself where o is a class, or each
// base of the class `super()` is in. One join per attribute node, which the lookup above, `need_attr`, `vopen` and
// the method resolution read, in place of each joining the object's values to the class's bindings itself.
.decl pt_alook(n: node, c: node, a: symbol)
pt_alook(n, c, a) :- pt_attr_of(n, o, a), pt_pv(o, "cls", c).
pt_alook(n, c, a) :- pt_attr_of(n, o, a), pt_pv(o, "inst", c).
pt_alook(n, b, a) :- pt_attr_of(n, o, a), pt_pv(o, "super", c), pt_base(c, b).
// pt_pass(n, c): n's value is c's (a parenthesized value, either branch of a conditional, either operand of `and`/`or`,
// an assignment's right side, a walrus's value).
.decl pt_pass(n: node, c: node)
pt_pass(n, c) :- kind(n, "parenthesized_expression"), child(n, c, 0).
pt_pass(n, c) :- kind(n, "conditional_expression"), child(n, c, 0).
pt_pass(n, c) :- kind(n, "conditional_expression"), child(n, c, 2).
pt_pass(n, c) :- kind(n, "boolean_operator"), field(n, "left", c).
pt_pass(n, c) :- kind(n, "boolean_operator"), field(n, "right", c).
pt_pass(n, c) :- kind(n, "assignment"), field(n, "right", c).
pt_pass(n, c) :- kind(n, "named_expression"), field(n, "value", c).
pt_pv(n, k, v) :- pt_pass(n, c), pt_pv(c, k, v).
// Calls: a class makes an instance; a function returns what its returns hold, or the argument it returns.
pt_pv(c, "inst", k) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "cls", k).
// pt_cfn(c, e, f): call c of e runs f, a function, or an overload its positional arguments fit (`iter(x)` is not typed
// by `iter(f, sentinel)`). A call with a splat, a generator argument or more than eight positional arguments fits every
// overload, and one with keywords every overload with room for its positional arguments. A method's `self` is bound
// by an attribute call.
.decl pt_cfn(c: node, e: node, f: node)
pt_cfn(c, e, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "fn", f), !pt_ovlfn(f).
pt_cfn(c, e, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "fn", f), pt_ovlfn(f), pt_cwild(c).
pt_cfn(c, e, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "fn", f), pt_ovlfn(f), !pt_method(f, _), pt_cposk(c, n, w), pt_ffit(f, n, w).
pt_cfn(c, e, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "fn", f), pt_ovlfn(f), pt_method(f, _), !pt_attr_of(e, _, _), pt_cposk(c, n, w), pt_ffit(f, n, w).
pt_cfn(c, e, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "fn", f), pt_ovlfn(f), pt_method(f, _), pt_attr_of(e, _, _), pt_cposk(c, m, w), pt_pred(n, m), pt_ffit(f, n, w).
.decl pt_ovlfn(f: node)
pt_ovlfn(f) :- pt_ovlstmt(st), field(st, "definition", f).
.decl pt_cwild(c: node)
pt_cwild(c) :- pt_posarg(c, 8, _).
pt_cwild(c) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "arguments", as), child(as, a, _), kind(a, "list_splat").
pt_cwild(c) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "arguments", as), child(as, a, _), kind(a, "dictionary_splat").
pt_cwild(c) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "arguments", g), kind(g, "generator_expression").
.decl pt_ckw(c: node)
pt_ckw(c) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "arguments", as), child(as, a, _), kind(a, "keyword_argument").
// pt_cpos(c, n): c has n positional arguments.
.decl pt_cpos(c: node, n: number)
pt_cpos(c, 0) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "arguments", as), kind(as, "argument_list"), !pt_posarg(c, _, _), !pt_cwild(c).
pt_cpos(c, n) :- pt_posarg(c, j, _), !pt_posarg(c, n, _), pt_pred(n, j), !pt_cwild(c).
// pt_cposk(c, n, w): c has n positional arguments, and keywords (w = 1) or none (w = 0).
.decl pt_cposk(c: node, n: number, w: number)
pt_cposk(c, n, 1) :- pt_cpos(c, n), pt_ckw(c).
pt_cposk(c, n, 0) :- pt_cpos(c, n), !pt_ckw(c).
// pt_ffit(f, n, w): n positional arguments, with keywords (w = 1) or without, fit overload f: at least its required ones
// and none of its keyword-only ones
// required (unless keywords may give them), at most its positional ones (unless it takes `*args`). Per overload, not
// per call: a call's fit is a lookup.
.decl pt_ffit(f: node, n: number, w: number)
pt_ffit(f, n, 0) :- pt_ovlfn(f), pt_slot(n), pt_fneed(f, r), r <= n, pt_fcap(f, p), n <= p, !pt_fkwreq(f).
pt_ffit(f, n, 1) :- pt_ovlfn(f), pt_slot(n), pt_fcap(f, p), n <= p.
.decl pt_slot(n: number)
pt_slot(0). pt_slot(1). pt_slot(2). pt_slot(3). pt_slot(4). pt_slot(5). pt_slot(6). pt_slot(7). pt_slot(8). pt_slot(9).
// An overload's parameters by position (`self` counted, `/` not), before any `*`, `*args` or `**kw`.
.decl pt_pstar(f: node, k: number)
pt_pstar(f, k) :- pt_ovlfn(f), field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, k), kind(p, "keyword_separator").
pt_pstar(f, k) :- pt_ovlfn(f), field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, k), kind(p, "list_splat_pattern").
pt_pstar(f, k) :- pt_ovlfn(f), field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, k), kind(p, "dictionary_splat_pattern").
pt_pstar(f, k) :- pt_ovlfn(f), field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, k), kind(p, "typed_parameter"), child(p, s, 0), kind(s, "list_splat_pattern").
pt_pstar(f, k) :- pt_ovlfn(f), field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, k), kind(p, "typed_parameter"), child(p, s, 0), kind(s, "dictionary_splat_pattern").
.decl pt_pstar_before(f: node, k: number)
pt_pstar_before(f, k) :- pt_pstar(f, s), pt_ovlfn(f), field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, _, k), s <= k.
.decl pt_psep_before(f: node, k: number)
pt_psep_before(f, k) :- pt_ovlfn(f), field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, q, s), kind(q, "positional_separator"), child(ps, _, k), s < k.
.decl pt_ppos(f: node, i: number, p: node)
pt_ppos(f, k, p) :- pt_ovlfn(f), field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, k), !kind(p, "positional_separator"), !pt_pstar_before(f, k),
    !pt_psep_before(f, k).
pt_ppos(f, i, p) :- pt_ovlfn(f), field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, k), !kind(p, "positional_separator"), !pt_pstar_before(f, k),
    pt_psep_before(f, k), pt_pred(k, i).
.decl pt_preq(f: node, i: number)
pt_preq(f, i) :- pt_ppos(f, i, p), kind(p, "identifier").
pt_preq(f, i) :- pt_ppos(f, i, p), kind(p, "typed_parameter").
.decl pt_fneed(f: node, n: number)
pt_fneed(f, 0) :- pt_ovlfn(f), !pt_preq(f, _).
pt_fneed(f, n) :- pt_preq(f, i), pt_pred(n, i), !pt_preq(f, n).
.decl pt_fkwreq(f: node)
pt_fkwreq(f) :- pt_ovlfn(f), field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, k), pt_pstar_before(f, k), !pt_pstar(f, k), kind(p, "identifier").
pt_fkwreq(f) :- pt_ovlfn(f), field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, k), pt_pstar_before(f, k), !pt_pstar(f, k), kind(p, "typed_parameter").
.decl pt_fstar(f: node)
pt_fstar(f) :- pt_ovlfn(f), field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, _), kind(p, "list_splat_pattern").
pt_fstar(f) :- pt_ovlfn(f), field(f, "parameters", ps), child(ps, p, _), kind(p, "typed_parameter"), child(p, s, 0), kind(s, "list_splat_pattern").
.decl pt_fcap(f: node, n: number)
pt_fcap(f, 9) :- pt_fstar(f).
pt_fcap(f, 0) :- pt_ovlfn(f), !pt_fstar(f), !pt_ppos(f, _, _).
pt_fcap(f, n) :- pt_ppos(f, i, _), pt_pred(n, i), !pt_ppos(f, n, _), !pt_fstar(f).
pt_pv(c, k, v) :- pt_cfn(c, e, f), !pt_isasync(f), !pt_isgen(f), pt_fret(f, k, v).
// pt_fret(f, k, v): function f may return a k v.
.decl pt_fret(f: node, k: symbol, v: node)
pt_fret(f, k, v) :- pt_retval(f, r), pt_pv(r, k, v).
pt_pv(c, k, v) :- pt_cfn(c, e, f), !pt_method(f, _), pt_retparam(f, i, _), pt_posarg(c, i, a), pt_pv(a, k, v).
pt_pv(c, "super", k) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_builtin_ref(e, "super"), nearest(c, f, pt_fdef), pt_method(f, k).
// The standard library's `builtins`, where a run loads it (t21): a builtin name is that module's binding of the name
// (`super` keeps its own value above), and a literal is an instance of its builtins class. Not `object`: every class
// is one, so a value declared `object` is any instance at all, which is no knowledge (and every class's rows).
// Each with its qualified name made first (`bq`, `litq`), so the join with `qv` is on that name.
.decl pt_bq(n: node, q: symbol)
pt_bq(n, q) :- pt_builtin_ref(n, x), x != "super", x != "object", q = @dot("builtins", x).
pt_lv(n, k, v) :- pt_bq(n, q), pt_lres(q, d), pt_lval(d, k, v).
// `object` as an attribute's receiver (`object.__getattribute__(v, "x")`, `object.__setattr__`) is the class itself, one
// definite value: its methods are the attribute.
pt_lv(o, "cls", "builtins.object") :- pt_attr_of(_, o, _), pt_builtin_ref(o, "object"), struct__def("builtins.object", "class").
.decl pt_lit_cls(kind: symbol, q: symbol)
pt_lit_cls("integer", "builtins.int"). pt_lit_cls("float", "builtins.float"). pt_lit_cls("string", "builtins.str").
pt_lit_cls("concatenated_string", "builtins.str"). pt_lit_cls("true", "builtins.bool"). pt_lit_cls("false", "builtins.bool").
pt_lit_cls("list", "builtins.list"). pt_lit_cls("list_comprehension", "builtins.list"). pt_lit_cls("dictionary", "builtins.dict").
pt_lit_cls("dictionary_comprehension", "builtins.dict"). pt_lit_cls("set", "builtins.set"). pt_lit_cls("set_comprehension", "builtins.set").
pt_lit_cls("tuple", "builtins.tuple").
.decl pt_litq(n: node, q: symbol)
pt_litq(n, q) :- pt_vpos(n), kind(n, k), pt_lit_cls(k, q), !pt_bytes_lit(n).
pt_litq(n, "builtins.bytes") :- pt_bytes_lit(n).
pt_lv(n, "inst", c) :- pt_litq(n, q), pt_lres(q, c), struct__def(c, "class").

// ---- library values, by symbol (P2's exports) --------------------------------------------------------------------
// pt_wsmod(q): a module of this phase's documents, the workspace's. A symbol whose module is another is a library's.
.decl pt_wsmod(q: symbol)
pt_wsmod(q) :- pt_modname(_, q).
.decl pt_wsown(d: symbol)
pt_wsown(d) :- types__owner(d, m), pt_wsmod(m).
// pt_lres(q, d): the qualified name q (an import, a dotted name read from one, a builtin) is symbol d: a module, else a
// module's name (through its imports and re-exports, `types__binds`), else a class's (through its bases).
.decl pt_lwant(q: symbol)
pt_lwant(q) :- pt_qn(_, q).
pt_lwant(q) :- pt_ibind(_, _, q).
pt_lwant(q) :- pt_bq(_, q).
pt_lwant(q) :- pt_litq(_, q).
pt_lwant(q) :- pt_star_from(_, q).
pt_lwant(p) :- pt_lwant(q), split_dot(q, p, _).
.decl pt_lres(q: symbol, d: symbol)
pt_lres(q, q) :- pt_lwant(q), struct__def(q, "module").
pt_lres(q, d) :- pt_lwant(q), !struct__def(q, "module"), split_dot(q, p, y), !contains(".", y), pt_lres(p, m), struct__def(m, "module"), types__binds(m, y, d).
pt_lres(q, d) :- pt_lwant(q), !struct__def(q, "module"), split_dot(q, p, y), !contains(".", y), pt_lres(p, c), struct__def(c, "class"), types__attr(c, y, d, _), d != "".
// pt_lval(d, k, v): library symbol d's value: a module, a class or a function (itself), or a name declared a class's
// instance (`x: C`), or None.
.decl pt_lval(d: symbol, k: symbol, v: symbol)
pt_lval(d, "mod", d) :- struct__def(d, "module"), !pt_wsown(d).
pt_lval(d, "cls", d) :- struct__def(d, "class"), !pt_wsown(d).
pt_lval(d, "fn", d) :- struct__def(d, "function"), !pt_wsown(d).
pt_lval(d, "inst", c) :- types__vtype(d, _, c), struct__def(c, "class"), !struct__def(d, _), !pt_wsown(d).
pt_lval(d, "none", "builtins.None") :- types__vtype(d, _, "builtins.None"), !struct__def(d, _), !pt_wsown(d).
// pt_lret(f, k, v): a call of library function f holds an instance of its declared return's class (each of a union's), or
// None.
.decl pt_lret(f: symbol, k: symbol, v: symbol)
// Not an `async def`'s: its call holds a coroutine (open, as a workspace one's).
pt_lret(f, "inst", t) :- types__rtype(f, _, t), struct__def(t, "class"), !struct__flag(f, "async").
pt_lret(f, "none", "builtins.None") :- types__rtype(f, _, "builtins.None"), !struct__flag(f, "async").
// pt_lopenret(f): some alternative of f's declared return is no class nor None (`Any`, a type variable, a name no
// symbol gives; types.rerail's "" row): a call of f may hold what no symbol names. pt_lopenv(s): so is s's declared type.
.decl pt_lopenret(f: symbol)
pt_lopenret(f) :- types__ropen(f), !pt_lself(f).
.decl pt_lopenv(s: symbol)
pt_lopenv(s) :- types__vtype(s, _, ""), !struct__def(s, _).
.decl pt_lself(f: symbol)
pt_lself(f) :- types__rtype(f, _, "typing.Self").
pt_lself(f) :- types__rtype(f, _, "typing_extensions.Self").
// A decorator declared to return its argument's own type, `(f: F) -> F` with F no class (a type variable).
.decl pt_lident(g: symbol)
pt_lident(g) :- types__sig(g, 0, _, a, d), d != "", !struct__def(d, _), types__rtype(g, a, _), match("^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z_0-9]*$", a).
// A decorator declared `(f: Callable[P, A]) -> Callable[P, B]`: its result calls f and holds a B (`types__callret`).
.decl pt_lwrap(g: symbol, b: symbol)
pt_lwrap(g, b) :- types__sig(g, 0, _, a, _), match("^([A-Za-z_.]*\\.)?Callable\\[(?<p>[A-Za-z_0-9]+), .*$", a), types__callret(g, _, b),
    types__rtype(g, r, _), match("^([A-Za-z_.]*\\.)?Callable\\[(?<q>[A-Za-z_0-9]+), .*$", r), p = q.

// What a scope's names hold of a library's: an import, an assignment, a star import, a workspace module's re-export.
.decl pt_lbv(s: node, x: symbol, k: symbol, v: symbol)
.decl pt_lqv(m: node, q: symbol, k: symbol, v: symbol)
pt_lbv(s, x, k, v) :- pt_ibind(s, x, q), pt_lres(q, d), pt_lval(d, k, v).
pt_lbv(s, x, k, v) :- pt_ibind(s, x, q), pt_wres(q, w), pt_lqv(_, w, k, v).
pt_lbv(s, x, k, v) :- pt_live_asg(s, x, r), pt_lv(r, k, v).
pt_lbv(m, x, k, v) :- pt_starx(m, x, d), pt_wkey(d, w), pt_lqv(_, w, k, v).
pt_lbv(m, x, k, v) :- pt_starx(m, x, d), pt_lval(d, k, v).
pt_lqv(m, @dot(q, x), k, v) :- pt_modname(m, q), pt_lbv(m, x, k, v).
// Annotations naming a library's class (`p: Path`, `-> ContextVar[bool]`, `x: Pattern[str]` in a class body): its
// instances; `type[C]`: its class.
.decl pt_linst(t: node, c: symbol)
pt_linst(t, c) :- pt_aleaf(t, m), pt_ahead(m, h), pt_lv(h, "cls", c), !pt_builtin_ref(h, "type").
.decl pt_lcls(t: node, c: symbol)
pt_lcls(t, c) :- pt_aleaf(t, m), pt_ahead(m, h), pt_builtin_ref(h, "type"), pt_aarg(m, a), pt_lv(a, "cls", c).
pt_lbv(f, x, "inst", c) :- pt_pann(f, x, t), pt_pread(f, x), pt_linst(t, c).
pt_lbv(f, x, "cls", c) :- pt_pann(f, x, t), pt_pread(f, x), pt_lcls(t, c).
pt_lbv(c, x, "inst", k) :- pt_cann(c, x, t), pt_cread(c, x), pt_linst(t, k).
pt_lbv(c, x, "cls", k) :- pt_cann(c, x, t), pt_cread(c, x), pt_lcls(t, k).
pt_lv(c, "inst", k) :- pt_cfn(c, _, f), pt_rann(f, t), !pt_isasync(f), pt_linst(t, k).
pt_lv(c, "cls", k) :- pt_cfn(c, _, f), pt_rann(f, t), !pt_isasync(f), pt_lcls(t, k).
pt_lv(c, "inst", k) :- pt_ifn(c, f), pt_rann(f, t), !pt_isasync(f), pt_linst(t, k).
// A library protocol's instances need not derive from it.
.decl pt_lproto(c: symbol)
pt_lproto(c) :- struct__base(c, _, b), match("^([A-Za-z_.]*\\.)?Protocol(\\[.*)?$", b).
// A library decorator: the definition kept (`(f: F) -> F`), or what the decorator returns.
pt_bv(s, x, k, f) :- pt_live_def(s, x, f), pt_dec1(f, e), pt_lv(e, "fn", g), pt_lident(g), pt_defk(f, k).
pt_bv(s, x, "wfn", f) :- pt_live_def(s, x, f), pt_dec1(f, e), pt_lv(e, "fn", g), pt_lwrap(g, _), !pt_lident(g).
pt_lbv(s, x, k, v) :- pt_live_def(s, x, f), pt_dec1(f, e), pt_lv(e, "fn", g), !pt_lident(g), !pt_lwrap(g, _), pt_lret(g, k, v).
.decl pt_ldec_known(f: node)
pt_ldec_known(f) :- pt_dec1(f, e), pt_lv(e, "fn", g), pt_lident(g).
pt_ldec_known(f) :- pt_dec1(f, e), pt_lv(e, "fn", g), pt_lwrap(g, _).
pt_ldec_known(f) :- pt_dec1(f, e), pt_lv(e, "fn", g), pt_lret(g, _, _).

.decl pt_lv(n: node, k: symbol, v: symbol)
pt_lv(n, k, v) :- pt_look(n, x, s), pt_lbv(s, x, k, v).
pt_lv(n, k, v) :- pt_qn(n, q), pt_lres(q, d), pt_lval(d, k, v).
pt_lv(n, k, v) :- pt_pass(n, c), pt_lv(c, k, v).
pt_lv(n, k, v) :- pt_attr_of(n, o, a), pt_lv(o, "mod", m), types__binds(m, a, d), pt_lval(d, k, v).
pt_lv(n, "mod", q) :- pt_attr_of(n, o, a), pt_lv(o, "mod", m), q = @dot(m, a), struct__def(q, "module").
// A workspace class's attribute that holds a library's value (`pattern = re.compile(...)`, `x: Path`).
pt_lv(n, k, v) :- pt_alook(n, c, a), pt_found(c, a, at), pt_lbv(at, a, k, v).
// An attribute of a library class or instance: the class's own or a base's (`types__attr`); an attribute assigned in
// a class body is what it is declared (`x: int`).
.decl pt_llook(n: node, c: symbol, a: symbol)
pt_llook(n, c, a) :- pt_attr_of(n, o, a), pt_lv(o, "inst", c).
pt_llook(n, c, a) :- pt_attr_of(n, o, a), pt_lv(o, "cls", c).
.decl pt_lattr(n: node, k: symbol, v: symbol)
pt_lattr(n, k, v) :- pt_llook(n, c, a), types__attr(c, a, d, _), d != "", pt_lval(d, k, v).
pt_lattr(n, "inst", t) :- pt_llook(n, c, a), types__attr(c, a, "", kc), s = @dot(kc, a), pt_ldecl(s, t).
// pt_ldecl(s, t): library symbol s is declared an instance of class t.
.decl pt_ldecl(s: symbol, t: symbol)
pt_ldecl(s, t) :- types__vtype(s, _, t), struct__def(t, "class").
pt_lv(n, k, v) :- pt_lattr(n, k, v).
// A workspace class's library bases, and the names it reaches through them (as `found`, union over the bases).
.decl pt_lbase(c: node, b: symbol)
pt_lbase(c, b) :- pt_basex(c, e), pt_lv(e, "cls", b).
pt_lbase(c, b) :- pt_basex(c, e), kind(e, "subscript"), field(e, "value", g), pt_lv(g, "cls", b).
.decl pt_lfound(c: node, a: symbol, b: symbol)
pt_lfound(c, a, b) :- pt_lbase(c, b), !pt_bound_in(c, a), types__attr(b, a, _, _).
pt_lfound(c, a, b) :- pt_base(c, w), !pt_bound_in(c, a), pt_lfound(w, a, b).
.decl pt_lwlook(n: node, b: symbol, a: symbol)
pt_lwlook(n, b, a) :- pt_alook(n, c, a), pt_lfound(c, a, b).
pt_lwlook(n, b, a) :- pt_attr_of(n, o, a), pt_pv(o, "super", c), pt_lbase(c, b).
pt_lwlook(n, b, a) :- pt_attr_of(n, o, a), pt_pv(o, "super", c), pt_base(c, w), pt_lfound(w, a, b).
pt_lv(n, k, v) :- pt_lwlook(n, b, a), types__attr(b, a, d, _), d != "", pt_lval(d, k, v).
// Calls: a library class makes its instance, a library function holds what it is declared to return, an instance
// what its `__call__` does; a method declared `-> Self` its receiver.
pt_lv(c, "inst", k) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_lv(e, "cls", k).
pt_lv(c, k, v) :- pt_lcfn(c, e, f), pt_lret(f, k, v).
// pt_lcfn(c, e, f): call c of e runs library function f, or an overload of it its positional arguments fit (as `cfn`,
// by the overload's `struct__shape`): `os.environ.get(k)` is not typed by `get(k, default: T)`. A method's `self` is
// bound by an attribute call.
.decl pt_lcfn(c: node, e: node, f: symbol)
pt_lcfn(c, e, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_lv(e, "fn", f), !struct__flag(f, "overload").
pt_lcfn(c, e, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_lv(e, "fn", f), struct__flag(f, "overload"), pt_cwild(c).
pt_lcfn(c, e, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_lv(e, "fn", f), struct__flag(f, "overload"), !pt_lmethod(f), pt_cposk(c, n, w), pt_lfit(f, n, w), !pt_lnone(c, f, 0),
    !pt_lkwbad(c, f), !pt_ltybad(c, f, 0).
pt_lcfn(c, e, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_lv(e, "fn", f), struct__flag(f, "overload"), pt_lmethod(f), !pt_attr_of(e, _, _), pt_cposk(c, n, w), pt_lfit(f, n, w), !pt_lnone(c, f, 0),
    !pt_lkwbad(c, f), !pt_ltybad(c, f, 0).
pt_lcfn(c, e, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_lv(e, "fn", f), struct__flag(f, "overload"), pt_lmethod(f), pt_attr_of(e, _, _), pt_cposk(c, m, w), pt_pred(n, m), pt_lfit(f, n, w), !pt_lnone(c, f, 1),
    !pt_lkwbad(c, f), !pt_ltybad(c, f, 1).
// pt_lkwbad(c, f): call c names a keyword that overload f has no parameter of, and f takes no `**kwargs`
// (`os.environ.get(k, default=d)` is not `get(self, key, /)`). By the call's name, as `lnone`.
.decl pt_lkwbad(c: node, f: symbol)
pt_lkwbad(c, f) :- pt_lovname(x, f), pt_cnamed(c, x), pt_ckwname(c, k), !pt_lpname(f, k), !struct__flag(f, "kwargs").
.decl pt_ckwname(c: node, k: symbol)
pt_ckwname(c, k) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "arguments", as), child(as, a, _), kind(a, "keyword_argument"), field(a, "name", n), text(n, k).
.decl pt_lpname(f: symbol, k: symbol)
pt_lpname(f, k) :- struct__flag(f, "overload"), struct__param(f, _, k, _).
// pt_lovname(x, f): overload f's name (`os._Environ.get#1`: `get`).
.decl pt_lovname(x: symbol, f: symbol)
pt_lovname(x, f) :- struct__flag(f, "overload"), x = @replace_all(f, "^.*\\.|#[0-9]+$", "").
// pt_ltybad(c, f, s): call c's positional argument, a literal of class k, is no instance of what overload f's parameter
// (s on: a method's `self`) declares: every alternative of the parameter names a class, none a protocol, and k is
// none of them nor derives from one (`int` passes for `float` and `complex`, as PEP 484 has it). Only literals: an
// argument's value read from this phase's values would make the fit depend on itself through a negation.
.decl pt_ltybad(c: node, f: symbol, s: number)
pt_ltybad(c, f, 0) :- pt_lovname(x, f), pt_cnamed(c, x), pt_posarg(c, p, a), pt_litcls(a, k), pt_lsigclosed(f, p), !pt_lsigok(f, p, k).
pt_ltybad(c, f, 1) :- pt_lovname(x, f), pt_cnamed(c, x), pt_pred(p, q), pt_posarg(c, q, a), pt_litcls(a, k), pt_lsigclosed(f, p), !pt_lsigok(f, p, k).
.decl pt_litcls(a: node, k: symbol)
pt_litcls(a, "builtins.str") :- kind(a, "string"), !pt_litbytes(a).
pt_litcls(a, "builtins.bytes") :- pt_litbytes(a).
.decl pt_litbytes(a: node)
pt_litbytes(a) :- kind(a, "string"), text(a, t), match("^[bB].*", t).
pt_litcls(a, "builtins.int") :- kind(a, "integer").
pt_litcls(a, "builtins.float") :- kind(a, "float").
pt_litcls(a, "builtins.bool") :- kind(a, "true").
pt_litcls(a, "builtins.bool") :- kind(a, "false").
pt_litcls(a, "builtins.list") :- kind(a, "list").
pt_litcls(a, "builtins.dict") :- kind(a, "dictionary").
pt_litcls(a, "builtins.set") :- kind(a, "set").
pt_litcls(a, "builtins.tuple") :- kind(a, "tuple").
.decl pt_litk(k: symbol)
pt_litk("builtins.str"). pt_litk("builtins.bytes"). pt_litk("builtins.int"). pt_litk("builtins.float"). pt_litk("builtins.bool").
pt_litk("builtins.list"). pt_litk("builtins.dict"). pt_litk("builtins.set"). pt_litk("builtins.tuple").
.decl pt_lsigclosed(f: symbol, p: number)
pt_lsigclosed(f, p) :- pt_lovname(_, f), types__sig(f, p, _, a, d), a != "", d != "", !types__sig(f, p, _, a, ""), !pt_lsigproto(f, p).
.decl pt_lsigproto(f: symbol, p: number)
pt_lsigproto(f, p) :- pt_lovname(_, f), types__sig(f, p, _, _, d), types__proto(d).
.decl pt_lsigok(f: symbol, p: number, k: symbol)
pt_lsigok(f, p, k) :- pt_lovname(_, f), types__sig(f, p, _, _, k), pt_litk(k).
pt_lsigok(f, p, k) :- pt_lovname(_, f), types__sig(f, p, _, _, d), pt_litk(k), types__anc(k, d).
pt_lsigok(f, p, "builtins.int") :- pt_lovname(_, f), types__sig(f, p, _, _, "builtins.float").
pt_lsigok(f, p, "builtins.int") :- pt_lovname(_, f), types__sig(f, p, _, _, "builtins.complex").
pt_lsigok(f, p, "builtins.float") :- pt_lovname(_, f), types__sig(f, p, _, _, "builtins.complex").
// pt_lnone(c, f, s): overload f declares a parameter None that call c gives a literal of another type (`setdefault(k, [])`
// is not `setdefault(key, default: None = None)`), its arguments shifted by s (a method's `self`). By the overload's
// name and the argument's position first: every overload with a None parameter against every literal argument is a
// cross product otherwise.
.decl pt_lnone(c: node, f: symbol, s: number)
pt_lnone(c, f, 0) :- pt_lnonep(x, p, f), pt_cnamed(c, x), pt_posarg(c, p, a), pt_lnotnone(a).
pt_lnone(c, f, 1) :- pt_lnonep(x, p, f), pt_cnamed(c, x), pt_pred(p, q), pt_posarg(c, q, a), pt_lnotnone(a).
.decl pt_lnonep(x: symbol, p: number, f: symbol)
pt_lnonep(x, p, f) :- types__sig(f, p, _, "None", _), pt_lovname(x, f).
.decl pt_cnamed(c: node, x: symbol)
pt_cnamed(c, x) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", e), kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, x).
pt_cnamed(c, x) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", e), kind(e, "attribute"), field(e, "attribute", n), text(n, x).
.decl pt_lnotnone(a: node)
pt_lnotnone(a) :- kind(a, k), pt_lit_kind(k).
.decl pt_lit_kind(k: symbol)
pt_lit_kind("list"). pt_lit_kind("dictionary"). pt_lit_kind("set"). pt_lit_kind("tuple"). pt_lit_kind("string"). pt_lit_kind("concatenated_string").
pt_lit_kind("integer"). pt_lit_kind("float"). pt_lit_kind("true"). pt_lit_kind("false"). pt_lit_kind("list_comprehension").
pt_lit_kind("dictionary_comprehension"). pt_lit_kind("set_comprehension"). pt_lit_kind("lambda").
// pt_lfit(f, n, w): n positional arguments, with keywords (w = 1) or without, fit overload f.
.decl pt_lfit(f: symbol, n: number, w: number)
pt_lfit(f, n, 0) :- struct__shape(f, r, p, 0), pt_slot(n), r <= n, n <= p.
pt_lfit(f, n, 1) :- struct__shape(f, _, p, _), pt_slot(n), n <= p.
// pt_lmethod(f): overloaded library function f is defined in a class. Asked only of overloads, so it starts from them:
// over every library function (splitting each symbol, in every chunk) it was the cold run's costliest stratum.
.decl pt_lmethod(f: symbol)
pt_lmethod(f) :- struct__flag(f, "overload"), struct__member(_, _, f).
.decl struct__member(c: symbol, x: symbol, t: symbol)
// A call that no overload fits is open: its overloads say nothing of it.
.decl pt_lunfit(c: node)
pt_lunfit(c) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_lv(e, "fn", f), struct__flag(f, "overload"), !pt_lcfn(c, e, _).
.decl pt_lcallf(c: node, f: symbol)
pt_lcallf(c, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_lv(e, "inst", t), types__attr(t, "__call__", f, _), f != "".
pt_lv(c, k, v) :- pt_lcallf(c, f), pt_lret(f, k, v).
pt_lv(c, "inst", t) :- pt_lcfn(c, e, f), pt_lself(f), pt_attr_of(e, o, _), pt_lv(o, "inst", t).
pt_pv(c, "inst", w) :- pt_lcfn(c, e, f), pt_lself(f), pt_attr_of(e, o, _), pt_pv(o, "inst", w).
// A call of a library-wrapped workspace function holds the wrapper's declared B.
pt_lv(c, "inst", b) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "wfn", f), pt_dec1(f, d), pt_lv(d, "fn", g), pt_lwrap(g, b), struct__def(b, "class").
// B is a generic whose argument j is A's type variable (`types__wgen`): f's declared return gives it, through its
// class's map to A's (`@contextmanager def opened() -> Iterator[V]` is a `_GeneratorContextManager[V]`).
// pt_lwbind(f, g, j, x): f, wrapped by g, gives B's argument j the annotation x.
.decl pt_lwbind(f: node, g: symbol, kb: symbol, j: number, x: node)
pt_lwbind(f, g, kb, j, x) :- pt_dec1(f, d), pt_lv(d, "fn", g), types__wgen(g, ka, i, kb, j), pt_rann(f, t), pt_ann(t, rf), pt_gann_head(rf, hf), pt_lv(hf, "cls", kf),
    types__tparam(ka, i, w), types__tmap(kf, i2, ka, w), pt_sarg(rf, i2, x).
.decl pt_lwgen(c: node, f: node, g: symbol)
pt_lwgen(c, f, g) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "wfn", f), pt_lwbind(f, g, _, _, _).
pt_lghcls(c, kb) :- pt_lwgen(c, f, g), pt_lwbind(f, g, kb, _, _).
pt_pv(c, "gen", c) :- pt_lwgen(c, _, _).
pt_garg(c, j, x) :- pt_lwgen(c, f, g), pt_lwbind(f, g, _, j, x).
// Implicit calls (`o[i]`, a loop, a `with`) on a library instance.
// pt_liawait(c, f): the library `async def` an awaited implicit call runs: c holds what f declares (a stub's
// `async def __aenter__(self) -> Self`). A plain def that returns an awaitable (`AsyncIterator.__anext__`) is open.
.decl pt_liawait(c: node, f: symbol)
pt_liawait(c, f) :- pt_iawait(c, o, a), pt_lv(o, "inst", t), types__attr(t, a, f, _), f != "", struct__flag(f, "async").
.decl pt_laret(f: symbol)
pt_laret(f) :- types__rtype(f, _, t), struct__def(t, "class").
pt_lv(c, "inst", t) :- pt_liawait(c, f), types__rtype(f, _, t), struct__def(t, "class").
pt_lv(c, "inst", t) :- pt_liawait(c, f), pt_lself(f), pt_iawait(c, o, _), pt_lv(o, "inst", t).
.decl pt_lical(c: node, f: symbol)
pt_lical(c, f) :- pt_icall(c, o, a), pt_lv(o, "inst", t), types__attr(t, a, f, _), f != "".
pt_lv(c, k, v) :- pt_lical(c, f), pt_lret(f, k, v).
pt_lv(c, "inst", t) :- pt_lical(c, f), pt_lself(f), pt_icall(c, o, _), pt_lv(o, "inst", t).
// Library generics: a workspace annotation naming a library generic class (`d: dict[str, C]`, `xs: list[C]`) is a
// generic value, as a workspace class's is (`gleaf`); a library method declared to return its class's type variable
// (`get(...) -> _VT | None`), called on one, holds what the value's argument binds it to, through the class's bases
// (`types__tmap`); one declared to return a generic of it (`__iter__() -> Iterator[_T]`) holds that generic, its
// argument bound (so a loop's `__next__` binds Iterator's `_T_co` to the list's argument).
.decl pt_lgleaf(t: node, m: node)
pt_lgleaf(t, m) :- pt_uann(t), pt_aleaf(t, m), pt_ahead(m, h), m != h, pt_lv(h, "cls", k), types__tparam(k, _, _).
pt_bv(f, x, "gen", m) :- pt_pann(f, x, t), pt_pread(f, x), pt_lgleaf(t, m).
pt_bv(c, x, "gen", m) :- pt_cann(c, x, t), pt_cread(c, x), pt_lgleaf(t, m).
// A workspace module's or function's annotated name (`_ctx: ContextVar[B | None] = ContextVar(...)`,
// `grouped: dict[str, list[V]] = {}`): its declared library generic, beside the value assigned.
.decl pt_wmann(m: node, x: symbol, t: node)
pt_wmann(m, x, t) :- kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", l), kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, x), field(a, "type", t), nearest(a, m, pt_scope),
    kind(m, "module"), !py_dead_at(a).
pt_wmann(m, x, t) :- kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", l), kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, x), field(a, "type", t), nearest(a, m, pt_scope),
    kind(m, "function_definition"), !py_dead_at(a).
pt_uann(t) :- pt_wmann(_, _, t).
pt_bv(m0, x, "gen", m) :- pt_wmann(m0, x, t), pt_lgleaf(t, m).
// pt_lghcls(v, k): generic value v (an annotation, or a call standing for the generic it returns) is of library class k.
.decl pt_lghcls(v: node, k: symbol)
pt_lghcls(m, k) :- pt_lgleaf(_, m), pt_ahead(m, h), pt_lv(h, "cls", k).
pt_lghcls(x, k) :- pt_sarg(_, _, x), pt_ghead(x, h), x != h, pt_lv(h, "cls", k), types__tparam(k, _, _).
pt_lghcls(c, k) :- pt_gfn(c, f), pt_rgen(f, r), pt_ahead(r, h), pt_lv(h, "cls", k).
pt_garg(m, i, x) :- pt_lghcls(m, _), pt_sarg(m, i, x).
pt_pv(c, "gen", c) :- pt_gfn(c, f), pt_rgen(f, _), pt_lghcls(c, _).
.decl pt_lgret(f: symbol)
pt_lgret(f) :- types__rvar(f, _).
pt_lgret(f) :- types__rgen(f, _, _, _).
// pt_lgcall(c, o, f): call c (a call, an implicit call) on o runs library method f, declared to return a type variable
// or a generic of one; pt_lclassof(f, a): f is class a's.
.decl pt_lgcall(c: node, o: node, f: symbol)
pt_lgcall(c, o, f) :- pt_lcfn(c, e, f), pt_lgret(f), pt_attr_of(e, o, _).
pt_lgcall(c, o, f) :- pt_lical(c, f), pt_lgret(f), pt_icall(c, o, _).
.decl pt_lclassof(f: symbol, a: symbol)
pt_lclassof(f, a) :- pt_lgret(f), struct__member(a, _, f).
// pt_lgpar(c, y, x): at call c, the receiver's generic value binds type variable y (a parameter of the method's class)
// to annotation x.
.decl pt_lgpar(c: node, y: symbol, x: node)
pt_lgpar(c, y, x) :- pt_lgcall(c, o, f), pt_lclassof(f, a), pt_pv(o, "gen", g), pt_lghcls(g, k), types__tmap(k, i, a, y), pt_garg(g, i, x).
.decl pt_lgbound(c: node, y: symbol)
pt_lgbound(c, y) :- pt_lgpar(c, y, _).
.decl pt_lgx(c: node, x: node)
pt_lgx(c, x) :- pt_lgcall(c, _, f), types__rvar(f, y), pt_lgpar(c, y, x).
pt_gbind(c, x) :- pt_lgx(c, x).
// A union argument (`ContextVar[B | None]`): each member, the workspace's classes with their subclasses (as `gcls`).
.decl pt_umem(e: node, m: node)
pt_umem(e, m) :- kind(e, "binary_operator"), op(e, "|"), field(e, "left", m).
pt_umem(e, m) :- kind(e, "binary_operator"), op(e, "|"), field(e, "right", m).
pt_umem(e, m) :- kind(e, "parenthesized_expression"), child(e, m, 0).
.decl pt_lgxu(c: node, m: node)
pt_lgxu(c, m) :- pt_lgx(c, e), pt_umem(e, m).
pt_lgxu(c, m) :- pt_lgxu(c, e), pt_umem(e, m).
pt_pv(c, "inst", s) :- pt_lgxu(c, m), pt_pv(m, "cls", k), pt_anc(s, k).
pt_lv(c, "inst", k) :- pt_lgxu(c, m), pt_lv(m, "cls", k).
pt_lv(c, "inst", k) :- pt_lgx(c, x), pt_ghead(x, h), pt_lv(h, "cls", k).
pt_pv(c, "gen", x) :- pt_lgx(c, x), pt_lghcls(x, _).
pt_lghcls(c, k) :- pt_lgcall(c, _, f), types__rgen(f, k, _, y), pt_lgpar(c, y, _).
pt_garg(c, j, x) :- pt_lgcall(c, _, f), types__rgen(f, _, j, y), pt_lgpar(c, y, x).
pt_pv(c, "gen", c) :- pt_lgcall(c, _, f), types__rgen(f, _, _, y), pt_lgpar(c, y, _).
// A generic value's argument may be a library class, held as its symbol (`pt_lgarg(g, i, d)`): a library function
// declared to return a generic of classes (`dir() -> list[str]`), or a library class built from such a value.
.decl pt_lgarg(g: node, i: number, d: symbol)
pt_lghcls(c, k) :- pt_lcfn(c, _, f), types__rcarg(f, k, _, _).
pt_lgarg(c, j, d) :- pt_lcfn(c, _, f), types__rcarg(f, _, j, d).
pt_pv(c, "gen", c) :- pt_lcfn(c, _, f), types__rcarg(f, _, _, _).
// A library class's call binds its type parameters from its constructor's arguments: `frozenset(xs)`, where
// `__new__(cls, iterable: Iterable[_T_co])` and xs is a `list[str]`, is a `frozenset[str]` (list's parameter 0 is
// Iterable's `_T_co`, `types__tmap`). pt_lccall(c, k, f): call c of library class k runs constructor f (`__new__` or
// `__init__` as k finds it), an overload its positional arguments fit (the class counted as the first).
.decl pt_lctor(k: symbol, f: symbol)
pt_lctor(k, f) :- types__attr(k, "__new__", f, _), types__pgen(f, _, _, _, _).
pt_lctor(k, f) :- types__attr(k, "__init__", f, _), types__pgen(f, _, _, _, _).
.decl pt_lccall(c: node, k: symbol, f: symbol)
pt_lccall(c, k, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_lv(e, "cls", k), pt_lctor(k, f), !struct__flag(f, "overload").
pt_lccall(c, k, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_lv(e, "cls", k), pt_lctor(k, f), struct__flag(f, "overload"), pt_cposk(c, m, w), pt_pred(n, m), pt_lfit(f, n, w).
// pt_lcbind(c, n, g, i): at c, k's parameter n is argument i of g, the generic value passed where the constructor
// declares a generic of that parameter.
.decl pt_lcbind(c: node, n: number, g: node, i: number)
pt_lcbind(c, n, g, i) :- pt_lccall(c, k, f), types__pgen(f, p, h, j, y), types__tparam(k, n, y), pt_pred(p, q), pt_posarg(c, q, a), pt_pv(a, "gen", g),
    pt_lghcls(g, k2), types__tparam(h, j, z), types__tmap(k2, i, h, z).
pt_lghcls(c, k) :- pt_lcbind(c, _, _, _), pt_lccall(c, k, _).
pt_pv(c, "gen", c) :- pt_lcbind(c, _, _, _).
pt_garg(c, n, x) :- pt_lcbind(c, n, g, i), pt_garg(g, i, x).
pt_lgarg(c, n, d) :- pt_lcbind(c, n, g, i), pt_lgarg(g, i, d).
// pt_lgpars(c, y, d): as `lgpar`, the receiver's generic value binds y to the library class d.
.decl pt_lgpars(c: node, y: symbol, d: symbol)
pt_lgpars(c, y, d) :- pt_lgcall(c, o, f), pt_lclassof(f, a), pt_pv(o, "gen", g), pt_lghcls(g, k), types__tmap(k, i, a, y), pt_lgarg(g, i, d).
pt_lgbound(c, y) :- pt_lgpars(c, y, _).
pt_lv(c, "inst", d) :- pt_lgcall(c, _, f), types__rvar(f, y), pt_lgpars(c, y, d).
pt_lghcls(c, k) :- pt_lgcall(c, _, f), types__rgen(f, k, _, y), pt_lgpars(c, y, _).
pt_lgarg(c, j, d) :- pt_lgcall(c, _, f), types__rgen(f, _, j, y), pt_lgpars(c, y, d).
pt_pv(c, "gen", c) :- pt_lgcall(c, _, f), types__rgen(f, _, _, y), pt_lgpars(c, y, _).
// For counting: a call that reaches a library's callable.
.decl pt_call_lib(c: node)
pt_call_lib(c) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_lv(e, "fn", _).
pt_call_lib(c) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_lv(e, "cls", _).
pt_call_lib(c) :- pt_lcallf(c, _).

// ---- unknown values -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Positions whose value is read: what `vopen` is asked about.
.decl pt_vpos(n: node)
// pt_vroot(e): where a value is read. A guest's (a quoted annotation's code) are not: only its names are read.
.decl pt_vroot(e: node)
pt_vroot(e) :- pt_callee(_, e).
pt_vroot(o) :- pt_attr_of(_, o, _).
pt_vroot(r) :- pt_asg(_, _, r, _).
pt_vroot(r) :- pt_retval(_, r).
pt_vroot(e) :- pt_dexpr(_, e).
pt_vroot(e) :- pt_basex(_, e).
pt_vroot(a) :- pt_posarg(_, _, a).
pt_vroot(v) :- pt_pdefault(_, _, v).
pt_vpos(e) :- pt_vroot(e), !host_node(e, _).
pt_vpos(c) :- pt_vpos(n), kind(n, "parenthesized_expression"), child(n, c, 0).
pt_vpos(c) :- pt_vpos(n), kind(n, "conditional_expression"), child(n, c, 0).
pt_vpos(c) :- pt_vpos(n), kind(n, "conditional_expression"), child(n, c, 2).
pt_vpos(c) :- pt_vpos(n), kind(n, "boolean_operator"), child(n, c, _).
pt_vpos(c) :- pt_vpos(n), kind(n, "assignment"), field(n, "right", c).
pt_vpos(c) :- pt_vpos(n), kind(n, "named_expression"), field(n, "value", c).
.decl pt_tracked(k: symbol)
pt_tracked("identifier"). pt_tracked("attribute"). pt_tracked("call"). pt_tracked("parenthesized_expression"). pt_tracked("conditional_expression").
pt_tracked("boolean_operator"). pt_tracked("assignment"). pt_tracked("named_expression").
// Values that are no workspace callable and whose methods are no workspace definition: literals and operators on them.
pt_tracked("integer"). pt_tracked("float"). pt_tracked("string"). pt_tracked("concatenated_string"). pt_tracked("true"). pt_tracked("false").
pt_tracked("none"). pt_tracked("subscript"). pt_tracked("for_statement"). pt_tracked("as_pattern_target"). pt_tracked("list"). pt_tracked("dictionary"). pt_tracked("set"). pt_tracked("tuple"). pt_tracked("list_comprehension").
pt_tracked("await"). pt_tracked("dictionary_comprehension"). pt_tracked("set_comprehension"). pt_tracked("comparison_operator"). pt_tracked("not_operator").
.decl pt_iattr(t: node, c: node, a: symbol)
pt_iattr(t, c, a) :- field(_, "left", t), kind(t, "attribute"), pt_attr_of(t, o, a), pt_pv(o, "inst", c).
pt_iattr(t, c, a) :- field(_, "left", t), kind(t, "attribute"), pt_attr_of(t, o, a), pt_pv(o, "cls", c).
// A base that is an external class (a qualified name the workspace does not define, or a builtin): what it holds is
// no workspace definition. Any other base that is not a workspace class is unknown.
.decl pt_extb(e: node)
pt_extb(e) :- pt_basex(_, e), pt_qn(e, q), !pt_xknown(e, q).
.decl pt_xknown(e: node, q: symbol)
pt_xknown(e, q) :- pt_basex(_, e), pt_qn(e, q), pt_wres(q, w), pt_qv(_, w, _, _).
pt_extb(e) :- pt_basex(_, e), pt_builtin_ref(e, _).
// A library class, or its generic as a subscript (`AbstractContextManager[None]`, `lgbase`): `lbase` answers for it.
pt_extb(e) :- pt_basex(_, e), pt_lv(e, "cls", _).
pt_extb(e) :- pt_lgbase(e).
.decl pt_lgbase(e: node)
pt_lgbase(e) :- pt_basex(_, e), kind(e, "subscript"), field(e, "value", g), pt_lv(g, "cls", _).
// A typing special form as a base (`Generic[T]`, `Protocol`, `TypedDict`): no class to read, and none needed, as the
// members are the class's own. In typeshed these are values (`Generic: type[_Generic]`), so they are named here.
.decl pt_special_base_q(q: symbol)
pt_special_base_q("typing.Generic"). pt_special_base_q("typing.Protocol"). pt_special_base_q("typing.TypedDict").
pt_special_base_q("typing_extensions.Generic"). pt_special_base_q("typing_extensions.Protocol").
pt_special_base_q("typing_extensions.TypedDict").
// A generic class as a base, `K[T]` (`os.PathLike[str]`, `Mapping[K, V]`): the class K. Not a special form: typeshed's
// `Generic: type[_Generic]` reads as `_Generic` or any subclass, and every `class X(Generic[T])` is one, so a special
// form read as a class makes each generic class a base of every other.
.decl pt_gbase(e: node, k: node)
pt_gbase(e, k) :- pt_basex(_, e), kind(e, "subscript"), field(e, "value", g), pt_pv(g, "cls", k), !pt_special_base(e).
pt_base(c, b) :- pt_basex(c, e), pt_gbase(e, b).
.decl pt_special_base(e: node)
pt_special_base(e) :- pt_basex(_, e), pt_qn(e, q), pt_special_base_q(q).
pt_special_base(e) :- pt_basex(_, e), kind(e, "subscript"), field(e, "value", g), pt_qn(g, q), pt_special_base_q(q).
pt_special_base(e) :- pt_basex(_, e), pt_ownq(e, q), pt_special_base_q(q).
pt_special_base(e) :- pt_basex(_, e), kind(e, "subscript"), field(e, "value", g), pt_ownq(g, q), pt_special_base_q(q).
pt_extb(e) :- pt_special_base(e).
.decl pt_base_open(c: node)
pt_base_open(c) :- pt_basex(c, e), pt_vopen(e), !pt_special_base(e), !pt_gbase(e, _), !pt_lgbase(e).
pt_base_open(c) :- pt_basex(c, e), !pt_pv(e, "cls", _), !pt_extb(e), !pt_gbase(e, _).
.decl pt_attr_open(n: node, c: node, a: symbol)
pt_attr_open(n, c, a) :- pt_asks(n, c, a), pt_found(c, a, at), pt_bopen(at, a).
pt_attr_open(n, c, a) :- pt_asks(n, c, a), pt_anc(c, b), pt_base_open(b).
pt_attr_open(n, c, a) :- pt_asks(n, c, a), pt_anc(c, b), pt_iattr(_, b, a), !pt_adeclared(c, a).
// Neither bound by a workspace class nor reachable through an external base: set dynamically, or an AttributeError.
pt_attr_open(n, c, a) :- pt_asks(n, c, a), !pt_found(c, a, _), !pt_ext_base_up(c), a != "__init__", a != "__call__".
// An attribute an external base supplies: calling it runs no workspace definition, but as a value (a receiver, an
// assigned value) it may be anything, a workspace class included (`cls.__class__`).
.decl pt_ext_attr(n: node)
pt_ext_attr(n) :- pt_alook(n, c, a), !pt_found(c, a, _), pt_ext_base_up(c).
.decl pt_ext_base_up(c: node)
pt_ext_base_up(c) :- pt_anc(c, b), pt_basex(b, e), pt_extb(e).
.decl pt_bopen(s: node, x: symbol)
pt_bopen(s, x) :- pt_otgt(s, x).
pt_bopen(f, x) :- pt_param(f, x, i), !pt_selfparam(f, i), !pt_pclosed(f, x).
pt_bopen(f, x) :- pt_pdefault(f, x, v), pt_vopen(v).
pt_bopen(s, x) :- pt_live_asg(s, x, r), pt_vopen(r).
pt_bopen(s, x) :- pt_ifrom(s, x, m, _), pt_wsmod(m), pt_ibind(s, x, q), pt_wres(q, w), pt_qopen(_, w).
pt_bopen(s, x) :- pt_ifrom(s, x, m, _), pt_wsmod(m), pt_ibind(s, x, q), !pt_bknown(s, q).
.decl pt_bknown(s: node, q: symbol)
pt_bknown(s, q) :- pt_ibind(s, _, q), pt_wres(q, w), pt_qv(_, w, _, _).
// Or a library's value it holds (`_ctx = contextvars.ContextVar(...)`): `lqv`, as P3 keeps no library node.
pt_bknown(s, q) :- pt_ibind(s, _, q), pt_wres(q, w), pt_lqv(_, w, _, _).
pt_bknown(s, q) :- pt_ibind(s, _, q), pt_lres(q, d), pt_lval(d, _, _).
pt_bopen(s, x) :- pt_live_def(s, x, f), pt_opaque_dec(f, _), !pt_dec1(f, _).
pt_bopen(s, x) :- pt_live_def(s, x, f), pt_dec1(f, e), !pt_pv(e, "fn", _), !pt_ldec_known(f).
pt_bopen(s, x) :- pt_live_def(s, x, f), pt_dec1(f, e), pt_vopen(e).
pt_bopen(s, x) :- pt_live_def(s, x, f), pt_decfn(f, g), !pt_ident_dec(g), !pt_wrap(g, _, _), pt_retval(g, r), !pt_retparam(g, 0, r), pt_vopen(r).
pt_bopen(s, x) :- pt_live_def(s, x, f), pt_decfn(f, g), !pt_ident_dec(g), !pt_wrap(g, _, _), !pt_retval(g, _).
// A property's value is what its getter returns.
pt_bopen(s, x) :- pt_live_def(s, x, f), pt_dexpr(f, e), pt_builtin_ref(e, "property").
.decl pt_selfparam(f: node, i: number)
pt_selfparam(f, 0) :- pt_method(f, _), !pt_isstatic(f).
// A workspace module's qualified name that it binds to nothing static (a star import may bind it), or binds openly.
.decl pt_qopen(m: node, q: symbol)
pt_qopen(m, @dot(q, x)) :- pt_modname(m, q), pt_bopen(m, x).

.decl pt_vopen(n: node)
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), kind(n, k), !pt_tracked(k).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_look(n, x, s), pt_bopen(s, x).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_miss(n, x), !pt_builtin_ref(n, x).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_qn(n, q), pt_wres(q, w), pt_qopen(_, w).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_attr_of(n, o, _), pt_qn(o, q), pt_wsmod(q), pt_qn(n, q2), !pt_vknown(n, q2).
.decl pt_vknown(n: node, q: symbol)
pt_vknown(n, q) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_attr_of(n, _, _), pt_qn(n, q), pt_wres(q, w), pt_qv(_, w, _, _).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_attr_of(n, o, _), pt_vopen(o).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_attr_of(n, o, _), kind(o, k), !pt_tracked(k).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_alook(n, c, a), pt_attr_open(n, c, a).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_attr_of(n, o, a), pt_pv(o, "super", c), pt_base_open(c).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_attr_of(n, o, _), pt_pv(o, "fn", _).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_attr_of(n, o, _), pt_pv(o, "wfn", _).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_ext_attr(n), !pt_callee(_, n).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_pass(n, c), !kind(n, "boolean_operator"), pt_vopen(c).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), kind(n, "boolean_operator"), child(n, c, _), pt_vopen(c).
// A call's value: unknown when the callee is, when no workspace definition is called (an external or builtin
// callable), when a workspace function's return is, and for coroutines and generators.
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_callee(c, e), pt_vopen(e).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_callee(c, e), !pt_pv(e, _, _), !pt_pv(c, "super", _), !pt_bcall(c, _), !pt_lv(e, _, _).
// A library call whose value is not declared (no return annotation, a type variable, a special form), or an
// instance's call with no `__call__`.
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_lcfn(c, _, f), !pt_lret(f, _, _), !pt_lself(f), !pt_lgbound(c, _).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_lcfn(c, _, f), pt_lopenret(f).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_lunfit(c).
// A library call declared to return a type variable nothing binds at it.
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_lcfn(c, _, f), types__rvar(f, y), !pt_lgbound(c, y).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_lical(c, f), types__rvar(f, y), !pt_lgbound(c, y).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_lcallf(c, f), types__rvar(f, y).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_lcallf(c, f), pt_lopenret(f).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_lical(c, f), pt_lopenret(f).
// A library name, attribute or declared value whose declared type is partly unknown.
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_qn(n, q), pt_lres(q, d), !pt_wsown(d), pt_lopenv(d).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_llook(n, c, a), types__attr(c, a, d, _), d != "", pt_lopenv(d).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_llook(n, c, a), types__attr(c, a, "", k), s = @dot(k, a), pt_lopenv(s).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_attr_of(n, o, a), pt_lv(o, "mod", m), types__binds(m, a, d), pt_lopenv(d).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_callee(c, e), pt_lv(e, "inst", t), !pt_lcallf(c, _).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_lcallf(c, f), !pt_lret(f, _, _), !pt_lself(f).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_callee(c, e), pt_lv(e, "mod", _).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_callee(c, e), pt_lv(e, "none", _).
// An attribute a library class does not have (set dynamically, or through a base no symbol names), and one of a
// library function.
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_llook(n, _, _), !pt_lattr(n, _, _).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_attr_of(n, o, _), pt_lv(o, "mod", _), !pt_lv(n, _, _).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_attr_of(n, o, _), pt_lv(o, "fn", _).
// A name an import binds to a library's value no symbol gives (an alias, `x = y` in a stub).
pt_vopen(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_qn(n, q), pt_lres(q, d), !pt_wsown(d), !pt_lv(n, _, _), !pt_pv(n, _, _).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_cfn(c, e, f), pt_isasync(f).
// `await c`: what the async def c runs returns (as a sync call's value); any other awaited value is open.
pt_vopen(w) :- pt_vpos(w), kind(w, "await"), !pt_awaitf(w, _, _).
pt_vopen(w) :- pt_vpos(w), pt_awaitf(w, c, _), pt_callee(c, e), pt_vopen(e).
pt_vopen(w) :- pt_vpos(w), pt_awaitf(w, _, f), !pt_aclosed(f), pt_retval(f, r), !pt_retparam(f, _, r), pt_vopen(r).
pt_vopen(w) :- pt_vpos(w), pt_awaitf(w, _, f), !pt_aclosed(f), pt_retparam(f, _, _).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_cfn(c, e, f), !pt_rclosed(f), pt_isgen(f).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_cfn(c, e, f), !pt_rclosed(f), pt_retval(f, r), !pt_retparam(f, _, r), pt_vopen(r).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_cfn(c, e, f), !pt_rclosed(f), pt_retparam(f, i, _), !pt_posarg(c, i, _).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_cfn(c, e, f), !pt_rclosed(f), pt_retparam(f, i, _), pt_posarg(c, i, a), pt_vopen(a).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_cfn(c, e, f), !pt_rclosed(f), pt_method(f, _), pt_retparam(f, _, _).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "inst", _).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "mod", _).
// An implicit call's value: unknown when its receiver is, when no workspace method is found, when the method's
// return is.
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_icall(c, o, _), pt_vopen(o).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_icall(c, _, _), !pt_ifn(c, _), !pt_lical(c, _).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_iawait(c, o, _), pt_vopen(o).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_iawait(c, _, _), !pt_iafn(c, _), !pt_liawait(c, _).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_iafn(c, f), !pt_aclosed(f), pt_retval(f, r), !pt_retparam(f, _, r), pt_vopen(r).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_iafn(c, f), !pt_aclosed(f), pt_retparam(f, _, _).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_liawait(c, f), !pt_laret(f), !pt_lself(f).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_lical(c, f), !pt_lret(f, _, _), !pt_lself(f), !pt_lgbound(c, _).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_icall(c, o, a), pt_pv(o, "inst", k), pt_attr_open(c, k, a).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_ifn(c, f), pt_isasync(f).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_ifn(c, f), !pt_rclosed(f), pt_isgen(f).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_ifn(c, f), !pt_rclosed(f), pt_retval(f, r), !pt_retparam(f, _, r), pt_vopen(r).
pt_vopen(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_ifn(c, f), !pt_rclosed(f), pt_method(f, _), pt_retparam(f, _, _).

// ---- call targets ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.decl call_target(c: node, f: node)
call_target(c, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "fn", f), !pt_mro_dropped(e, f).
call_target(c, f) :- pt_wcall(c, f, _).
call_target(c, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "dfn", f), !pt_mro_dropped(e, f).
call_target(c, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "wfn", f), pt_dec1(f, d), pt_lv(d, "fn", g), pt_lwrap(g, _).
// Method resolution order. `found` is the union over every base, depth first, so in a diamond (`class D(B, C)`,
// both from `A`) `D.who` finds `A.who` through `B` and `C.who` through `C`. C3 gives `C.who`. A definition found
// on a class that another candidate class subclasses is never the one called, so it is dropped here, at the
// call. Values (`pv`) still flow as the union: `pv` and `found` are one recursive component, where the negation
// cannot go. Candidates neither of which subclasses the other are left to C3's left-to-right merge, which this
// does not model: the call is unknown (`mro_ambiguous`), never both.
.decl pt_mro_cand(n: node, c: node, at: node)
pt_mro_cand(n, c, at) :- pt_alook(n, c, a), pt_found(c, a, at).
// Per receiver class c: a late-bound `self` may be several classes, each with its own resolution.
.decl pt_mro_shadowed(n: node, c: node, at: node)
pt_mro_shadowed(n, c, at) :- pt_mro_cand(n, c, at), pt_mro_cand(n, c, x), x != at, pt_anc(x, at).
.decl pt_mro_kept(n: node, f: node)
// pt_method_kind(k): a binding of kind k is a function a method lookup may find, its own or one under outside decorators.
.decl pt_method_kind(k: symbol)
pt_method_kind("fn"). pt_method_kind("dfn").
pt_mro_kept(n, f) :- pt_mro_cand(n, c, at), !pt_mro_shadowed(n, c, at), pt_attr_of(n, _, a), pt_bv(at, a, k, f), pt_method_kind(k).
.decl pt_mro_dropped(n: node, f: node)
pt_mro_dropped(n, f) :- pt_mro_cand(n, c, at), pt_mro_shadowed(n, c, at), pt_attr_of(n, _, a), pt_bv(at, a, k, f), pt_method_kind(k),
    !pt_mro_kept(n, f).
.decl pt_mro_ambiguous(n: node)
pt_mro_ambiguous(n) :- pt_mro_cand(n, c, x), pt_mro_cand(n, c, y), x != y, !pt_mro_shadowed(n, c, x), !pt_mro_shadowed(n, c, y).
call_target(c, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "cls", k), pt_found(k, "__init__", at), pt_bv(at, "__init__", "fn", f).
call_target(c, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "inst", k), pt_found(k, "__call__", at), pt_bv(at, "__call__", "fn", f).
// A class call also runs the class's `__new__` and its metaclass's `__call__`, where the workspace defines them.
call_target(c, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "cls", k), pt_found(k, "__new__", at), pt_bv(at, "__new__", "fn", f).
call_target(c, f) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "cls", k), pt_anc(k, b), pt_metacls(b, mc), pt_found(mc, "__call__", at), pt_bv(at, "__call__", "fn", f).
.decl pt_metacls(c: node, m: node)
pt_metacls(c, mc) :- kind(c, "class_definition"), field(c, "superclasses", al), child(al, kw, _), kind(kw, "keyword_argument"),
    field(kw, "name", nm), text(nm, "metaclass"), field(kw, "value", v), pt_pv(v, "cls", mc).
.decl call_open(c: node)
call_open(c) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_vopen(e).
call_open(c) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "cls", k), pt_attr_open(c, k, "__init__").
call_open(c) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "inst", k), pt_attr_open(c, k, "__call__").
call_open(c) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "mod", _).
call_open(c) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "super", _).
call_open(c) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_mro_ambiguous(e).
.decl pt_ext_import(s: node, x: symbol)
pt_ext_import(s, x) :- pt_rifrom(s, x, m, _), !pt_wsmod(m).
pt_ext_import(s, x) :- pt_ribind(s, x, q), !pt_rifrom(s, x, _, _), !pt_wsmod(q).

// ---- call chains ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The function whose body holds a call (a lambda's or a nested class body's calls are the enclosing function's).
.decl pt_owner(c: node, f: node)
pt_owner(c, f) :- kind(c, "call"), nearest(c, f, pt_fdef).
.decl pt_calls(f: node, g: node)
pt_calls(f, g) :- pt_owner(c, f), call_target(c, g).
.decl pt_calls_open(f: node)
pt_calls_open(f) :- pt_owner(c, f), call_open(c).
// W5 `ASYNC_BLOCKING`: an async function's call, outside `await`, of a sync function that reaches a blocking call
// through sync functions only (the native `calls` term with `through: sync`).
.decl pt_blocking(q: symbol)
pt_blocking("time.sleep"). pt_blocking("requests.get"). pt_blocking("subprocess.run").
.decl pt_dq(f: node, q: symbol)
pt_dq(f, @dot(m, x)) :- pt_modname(s, m), pt_live_def(s, x, f).
.decl pt_blocks(f: node)
pt_blocks(f) :- pt_owner(c, f), pt_callee(c, e), pt_qn(e, q), pt_blocking(q).
pt_blocks(f) :- pt_owner(c, f), call_target(c, g), pt_dq(g, q), pt_blocking(q).
.decl pt_reach_sync(f: node)
pt_reach_sync(f) :- pt_blocks(f), !pt_isasync(f).
pt_reach_sync(f) :- pt_calls(f, g), pt_reach_sync(g), !pt_isasync(f).
// Unknown: an open call on a sync path, where no path is known to reach.
.decl pt_open_sync(f: node)
pt_open_sync(f) :- pt_calls_open(f), !pt_isasync(f).
pt_open_sync(f) :- pt_calls(f, g), pt_open_sync(g), !pt_isasync(f).
.decl pt_in_await(c: node)
pt_in_await(c) :- kind(c, "call"), child(w, c, 0), kind(w, "await").
.decl pt_finding(rule: symbol, n: node)
pt_finding("ASYNC_BLOCKING", c) :- pt_owner(c, a), pt_isasync(a), !pt_in_await(c), call_target(c, g), pt_reach_sync(g).
.decl pt_async_open(c: node)
pt_async_open(c) :- pt_owner(c, a), pt_isasync(a), !pt_in_await(c), call_target(c, g), pt_open_sync(g), !pt_reach_sync(g).
pt_async_open(c) :- pt_owner(c, a), pt_isasync(a), !pt_in_await(c), call_open(c).
// The witness chain for a message: each step of a reaching path.
.decl pt_chain_step(f: node, g: node)
pt_chain_step(f, g) :- pt_calls(f, g), pt_reach_sync(g), pt_reach_sync(f).

.decl pt_builtin(x: symbol)
pt_builtin("abs"). pt_builtin("aiter"). pt_builtin("all"). pt_builtin("anext"). pt_builtin("any"). pt_builtin("ascii"). pt_builtin("bin").
pt_builtin("bool"). pt_builtin("breakpoint"). pt_builtin("bytearray"). pt_builtin("bytes"). pt_builtin("callable"). pt_builtin("chr").
pt_builtin("classmethod"). pt_builtin("compile"). pt_builtin("complex"). pt_builtin("delattr"). pt_builtin("dict"). pt_builtin("dir").
pt_builtin("divmod"). pt_builtin("enumerate"). pt_builtin("eval"). pt_builtin("exec"). pt_builtin("filter"). pt_builtin("float").
pt_builtin("format"). pt_builtin("frozenset"). pt_builtin("getattr"). pt_builtin("globals"). pt_builtin("hasattr"). pt_builtin("hash").
pt_builtin("help"). pt_builtin("hex"). pt_builtin("id"). pt_builtin("input"). pt_builtin("int"). pt_builtin("isinstance").
pt_builtin("issubclass"). pt_builtin("iter"). pt_builtin("len"). pt_builtin("list"). pt_builtin("locals"). pt_builtin("map"). pt_builtin("max").
pt_builtin("memoryview"). pt_builtin("min"). pt_builtin("next"). pt_builtin("object"). pt_builtin("oct"). pt_builtin("open"). pt_builtin("ord").
pt_builtin("pow"). pt_builtin("print"). pt_builtin("property"). pt_builtin("range"). pt_builtin("repr"). pt_builtin("reversed").
pt_builtin("round"). pt_builtin("set"). pt_builtin("setattr"). pt_builtin("slice"). pt_builtin("sorted"). pt_builtin("staticmethod").
pt_builtin("str"). pt_builtin("sum"). pt_builtin("super"). pt_builtin("tuple"). pt_builtin("type"). pt_builtin("vars"). pt_builtin("zip").
pt_builtin("__import__"). pt_builtin("__name__"). pt_builtin("__file__"). pt_builtin("__doc__"). pt_builtin("__spec__"). pt_builtin("__debug__").
pt_builtin("NotImplemented"). pt_builtin("Ellipsis"). pt_builtin("BaseException"). pt_builtin("Exception"). pt_builtin("ValueError").
pt_builtin("TypeError"). pt_builtin("KeyError"). pt_builtin("IndexError"). pt_builtin("AttributeError"). pt_builtin("RuntimeError").
pt_builtin("NotImplementedError"). pt_builtin("OSError"). pt_builtin("ImportError"). pt_builtin("StopIteration"). pt_builtin("LookupError").
pt_builtin("ArithmeticError"). pt_builtin("AssertionError"). pt_builtin("EOFError"). pt_builtin("FileNotFoundError").
pt_builtin("ModuleNotFoundError"). pt_builtin("NameError"). pt_builtin("OverflowError"). pt_builtin("PermissionError").
pt_builtin("RecursionError"). pt_builtin("UnicodeError"). pt_builtin("UnicodeDecodeError"). pt_builtin("UnicodeEncodeError").
pt_builtin("ZeroDivisionError"). pt_builtin("KeyboardInterrupt"). pt_builtin("SystemExit"). pt_builtin("Warning").
pt_builtin("DeprecationWarning"). pt_builtin("UserWarning"). pt_builtin("RuntimeWarning"). pt_builtin("EnvironmentError").
pt_builtin("IOError"). pt_builtin("BufferError"). pt_builtin("ConnectionError"). pt_builtin("TimeoutError"). pt_builtin("GeneratorExit").

// ---- types (decision 0047, point 3) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// What a rule reads of a value's type, at the positions whose value the program models (`vpos`: callees and
// receivers, assigned, returned and decorating values, arguments and bases). Three-valued, as calls are:
//   type_of(n, t)        n may hold a value whose class is t: a workspace class's qualified name, or a builtin's
//                        name (`int`, `str`, `None`, ...)
//   type_open(n)         n may also hold a value of a class not listed
//   proven_type(n, t)    `isinstance(n, t)` is true: every class n may hold is t or a subclass of it, and none is
//                        unlisted
//   possible_type(n, t)  `isinstance(n, t)` may be true: some listed class is t or a subclass of it
//   possible_open(n)     possible_type is incomplete: n may hold an unlisted class, or a listed class whose bases
//                        are not all known
// A rule's `possible: t` is `possible_type(n, t)` or `possible_open(n)`; `not proven: t` is `!proven_type(n, t)`.
// A workspace subclass is a closed world: an instance of a class code outside the workspace derives from a
// workspace class reaches the program only through an unknown value (a parameter, an external call).
.decl pt_lit_type(k: symbol, t: symbol)
pt_lit_type("integer", "int"). pt_lit_type("float", "float"). pt_lit_type("string", "str"). pt_lit_type("concatenated_string", "str").
pt_lit_type("true", "bool"). pt_lit_type("false", "bool"). pt_lit_type("none", "None").
pt_lit_type("list", "list"). pt_lit_type("list_comprehension", "list"). pt_lit_type("dictionary", "dict").
pt_lit_type("dictionary_comprehension", "dict"). pt_lit_type("set", "set"). pt_lit_type("set_comprehension", "set").
pt_lit_type("tuple", "tuple"). pt_lit_type("not_operator", "bool").
// A bytes literal: its prefix (`strprefix`, lowercased) has a `b` (`b"..."`, `rb"..."`); a concatenation's
// parts share their kind.
.decl pt_bprefix(p: symbol)
pt_bprefix("b"). pt_bprefix("rb"). pt_bprefix("br").
.decl pt_bytes_lit(n: node)
pt_bytes_lit(n) :- pt_vpos(n), kind(n, "string"), strprefix(n, p), pt_bprefix(p).
pt_bytes_lit(n) :- pt_vpos(n), kind(n, "concatenated_string"), child(n, c, 0), strprefix(c, p), pt_bprefix(p).
// A builtin class whose call makes a value of that class.
.decl pt_bclass(x: symbol)
pt_bclass("int"). pt_bclass("float"). pt_bclass("complex"). pt_bclass("str"). pt_bclass("bytes"). pt_bclass("bytearray"). pt_bclass("bool").
pt_bclass("list"). pt_bclass("dict"). pt_bclass("set"). pt_bclass("frozenset"). pt_bclass("tuple"). pt_bclass("object").
.decl pt_bcall(c: node, x: symbol)
pt_bcall(c, x) :- pt_callee(c, e), pt_builtin_ref(e, x), pt_bclass(x).
.decl pt_btype(v: node, t: symbol)
pt_btype(v, t) :- pt_tv(_, "builtin", v), kind(v, k), pt_lit_type(k, t), !pt_bytes_lit(v).
pt_btype(v, "bytes") :- pt_tv(_, "builtin", v), pt_bytes_lit(v).
pt_btype(v, x) :- pt_tv(_, "builtin", v), pt_bcall(v, x).
// Values of builtin and external classes (`pt_tv(n, k, v)`, read by the types only). `builtin`: a literal, or a call of a
// builtin class (`btype` gives v's class). `ext`: a value from outside the workspace (a name an import of an
// external module binds, a builtin name, an attribute of such a value, a comparison), whose class is not named. They
// flow as `pv`'s values do, so `x = str(y)` gives `x` the class `str`, and a name bound both to `None` and to an
// external import is known to hold more than `None`. `tv` reads `pv` and `pv` does not read it: the points-to
// component, which every attribute and cross-file join reads, holds only functions, classes, instances and modules.
.decl pt_tv(n: node, k: symbol, v: node)
.decl pt_tbv(s: node, x: symbol, k: symbol, v: node)
.decl pt_tqv(m: node, q: symbol, k: symbol, v: node)
pt_tv(n, "builtin", n) :- pt_vpos(n), kind(n, k), pt_lit_type(k, _).
pt_tv(c, "builtin", c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_bcall(c, _).
pt_tv(n, "ext", n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_builtin_ref(n, _).
pt_tv(n, "ext", n) :- pt_vpos(n), kind(n, "comparison_operator").
pt_tv(n, "ext", n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_lv(n, _, _).
pt_tv(n, "ext", n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_attr_of(n, o, _), pt_tv(o, "ext", _).
pt_tbv(s, x, "ext", s) :- pt_ext_import(s, x).
pt_tbv(s, x, k, v) :- pt_live_asg(s, x, r), pt_tv(r, k, v).
pt_tbv(s, x, k, v) :- pt_ibind(s, x, q), pt_wres(q, w), pt_tqv(_, w, k, v).
pt_tqv(m, @dot(q, x), k, v) :- pt_modname(m, q), pt_tbv(m, x, k, v).
pt_tv(n, k, v) :- pt_look(n, x, s), pt_tbv(s, x, k, v).
pt_tv(n, k, v) :- pt_qn(n, q), pt_wres(q, w), pt_tqv(_, w, k, v).
pt_tv(n, k, v) :- pt_alook(n, c, a), pt_found(c, a, at), pt_tbv(at, a, k, v).
pt_tv(n, k, v) :- pt_pass(n, c), pt_tv(c, k, v).
pt_tv(c, k, v) :- pt_cfn(c, e, f), !pt_isasync(f), !pt_isgen(f), pt_retval(f, r), pt_tv(r, k, v).
pt_tv(c, k, v) :- pt_cfn(c, e, f), !pt_method(f, _), pt_retparam(f, i, _), pt_posarg(c, i, a), pt_tv(a, k, v).
// A workspace class's qualified name: a module's class, or a class's class. Classes in a function have none.
.decl pt_cls_q(c: node, q: symbol)
pt_cls_q(c, @dot(m, x)) :- pt_modname(s, m), pt_rdefn(s, x, c), kind(c, "class_definition").
pt_cls_q(c, @dot(q, x)) :- pt_cls_q(o, q), pt_rdefn(o, x, c), kind(c, "class_definition").

.decl type_of(n: node, t: symbol)
type_of(n, q) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_pv(n, "inst", c), pt_cls_q(c, q).
type_of(n, t) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_tv(n, "builtin", v), pt_btype(v, t).
type_of(n, t) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_tv(n, "decl", m), pt_dtype(m, t).
// A class object's class is `type`, unless a metaclass may make it another: a `metaclass=` keyword, an external base
// (`enum.Enum`, `abc.ABC`) or a base that is no known class, on the class or an ancestor. A builtin base keeps `type`.
type_of(n, "type") :- pt_vpos(n), pt_pv(n, "cls", c), !pt_meta_open(c).
type_of(n, "module") :- pt_vpos(n), pt_pv(n, "mod", _).
type_of(n, "module") :- pt_ext_mod(n).
// A name an `import` statement binds to a module outside the workspace (`import asyncio`), where nothing else binds it.
.decl pt_ext_mod(n: node)
pt_ext_mod(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_look(n, x, s), pt_ext_import(s, x), !pt_rifrom(s, x, _, _), !pt_rasg(s, x, _, _), !pt_rdefn(s, x, _).
.decl pt_meta_open(c: node)
pt_meta_open(c) :- pt_anc(c, b), kind(b, "class_definition"), field(b, "superclasses", al), child(al, kw, _), kind(kw, "keyword_argument"),
    field(kw, "name", nm), text(nm, "metaclass").
pt_meta_open(c) :- pt_anc(c, b), pt_basex(b, e), pt_extb(e), !pt_builtin_ref(e, _).
pt_meta_open(c) :- pt_anc(c, b), pt_base_open(b).
.decl type_open(n: node)
type_open(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_vopen(n), !pt_ext_mod(n).
type_open(n) :- pt_vpos(n), !pt_vopen(n), !pt_pv(n, _, _), !pt_tv(n, _, _), !pt_ext_mod(n).
// Functions and `super()` objects are values the relations do not name a class for.
type_open(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_pv(n, k, _), k != "inst", k != "cls", k != "mod", k != "gen".
type_open(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_tv(n, "ext", _), !pt_ext_mod(n).
type_open(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_pv(n, "cls", c), pt_meta_open(c).
type_open(n) :- pt_vpos(n), pt_pv(n, "inst", c), !pt_cls_q(c, _).
// A class whose `__new__` or metaclass `__call__` the workspace defines may make something else than its instance.
type_open(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "cls", k), pt_found(k, "__new__", _).
type_open(c) :- pt_vpos(c), pt_callee(c, e), pt_pv(e, "cls", k), pt_anc(k, b), pt_metacls(b, _).
// Subclassing between the names `type_of` gives: a workspace class's workspace bases, its external bases by
// qualified name, and its builtin bases.
.decl pt_tsub(n: node, t: symbol, u: symbol)
pt_tsub(n, t, t) :- type_of(n, t).
pt_tsub(n, t, "object") :- type_of(n, t).
pt_tsub(n, "bool", "int") :- type_of(n, "bool").
pt_tsub(n, t, u) :- type_of(n, t), pt_cls_q(c, t), pt_anc(c, b), pt_cls_q(b, u).
pt_tsub(n, t, u) :- type_of(n, t), pt_cls_q(c, t), pt_anc(c, b), pt_basex(b, e), pt_qn(e, u), !pt_xknown(e, u).
pt_tsub(n, t, x) :- type_of(n, t), pt_cls_q(c, t), pt_anc(c, b), pt_basex(b, e), pt_builtin_ref(e, x).
// A listed class some of whose superclasses are unknown: a base that is no known class, or an external base
// (whose own bases the program does not read).
.decl pt_tsup_open(n: node, t: symbol)
pt_tsup_open(n, t) :- type_of(n, t), pt_cls_q(c, t), pt_anc(c, b), pt_base_open(b).
pt_tsup_open(n, t) :- type_of(n, t), pt_cls_q(c, t), pt_anc(c, b), pt_basex(b, e), pt_extb(e), !pt_builtin_ref(e, "object").
.decl pt_type_miss(n: node, u: symbol)
// u is a supertype of one of n's types and not of another. Every type of a proven n is a subtype of u, so
// u's candidates are any type's supertypes (no "first" type: a min over symbols has no order, 0483).
pt_type_miss(n, u) :- pt_tsub(n, t0, u), type_of(n, t0), type_of(n, t), !pt_tsub(n, t, u).
.decl proven_type(n: node, u: symbol)
proven_type(n, u) :- type_of(n, t), pt_tsub(n, t, u), !type_open(n), !pt_type_miss(n, u).
.decl possible_type(n: node, u: symbol)
possible_type(n, u) :- type_of(n, t), pt_tsub(n, t, u).
.decl possible_open(n: node)
possible_open(n) :- type_open(n).
possible_open(n) :- type_of(n, t), pt_tsup_open(n, t).
